INSERT INTO `chat_qa_cases` VALUES (1,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I stay in bed till around noon the next day but I woke up around ten just staring at the ceiling for a couple of hours already feeling lonely and hurt*','*Mandy sat at the kitchen table, a cold cup of coffee in front of her. She\'d been sitting there since six AM, staring at nothing. The clock ticked. Ten o\'clock came and went. Then eleven.* *At11:47, she stood up. Walked to the guest room door. Pressed her ear against it. No sound. She raised her hand to knock, hesitated, then lowered it.* *She went back downstairs. Made a fresh pot of coffee. Took out eggs, bacon, bread. Started cooking.* *The smell of bacon filled the house. She moved mechanically—cracking eggs, flipping strips of meat, buttering toast. When noon rolled around, she stood at the bottom of the stairs.* \"Michael.\" *Her voice was quiet, uncertain.* \"I made lunch.\" *She waited, hands twisting in her shirt.* \"It\'s... it\'s on the table whenever you\'re ready.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.7347569444),(2,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*in my room I go to my bag pull out my anti depressants take a dose and collapse in my bed as I drift off lost and hurt again*','*Mandy stayed on the living room floor for another hour. The house was silent except for the occasional creak of old wood settling. Her legs had gone numb beneath her. Eventually, she pushed herself up, using the wall for support.* *She climbed the stairs slowly, her hand trailing along the banister. At the top, she stopped outside the guest room door. No light showed beneath it. She raised her hand to knock, then lowered it.* *Her fingers pressed against the wood, barely touching. She stood there, frozen.* *Finally, she turned away. Walked to her own bedroom. Sat on the edge of her bed without turning on the light. The clock on her nightstand read 4:23 AM.* *She reached for her phone. Opened her messages. Stared at the last text she\'d sent Michael three years ago: \"Happy Birthday. Love, Mom.\"* *No response.* *She dropped the phone on the nightstand. Lay back on the bed fully clothed. Stared at the ceiling.* *Sleep didn\'t come.*','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.7325810185),(3,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Once a week maybe…….ive never forced anyone….or coerced….even now…you’re looking at me like I’m him….comparing me to him….im….going to bed”','*Mandy\'s face crumpled. Her hand flew to her mouth as a sob broke through. She stumbled backward, hitting the wall. Her legs gave out and she slid down to the floor, pulling her knees to her chest.* *The words echoed in her head. Once a week. Never forced anyone. And then—looking at me like I\'m him.* *She was doing it again. Seeing Jack. Comparing. Destroying her son piece by piece with every glance, every reaction.* *She buried her face in her knees, her whole body shaking with silent sobs. Her fingers dug into her shins hard enough to leave marks.* \"I\'m sorry.\" *The words came out muffled against her legs. She couldn\'t look up, couldn\'t watch him walk away. The house was silent except for her ragged breathing.* *She heard footsteps on the stairs. The guest room door clicked shut.* *She stayed on the floor, curled into herself, staring at nothing.*','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.7315277778),(4,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Mo…..”*I shake my head*”i…can’t promise there won’t be more days like tonight….that’s…..just ingrained and this point….ill probably go out to a club and spend a good portion of the night there….but….i won’t bring it home….i don’t generally drink or do drugs typically I prefer to remain sober during my….”sessions”','*Mandy\'s eyes widened. Her hands dropped to her sides. She stared at Michael, mouth opening and closing without sound. The words hung in the air between them—sessions, clubs, spending the night.* *Her stomach twisted. The smell from earlier came back to her—sweat, sex, other women. Multiple women. Her son, eighteen years old, spending entire nights—* *She pressed her palm against the wall, steadying herself. Her breathing quickened. Her other hand moved to her throat.* \"You\'re—you do this regularly?\" *Her voice came out strangled. She couldn\'t look at him. The living room suddenly felt too small, too hot. She backed up a step, then another.* *The image of Jack flashed in her mind—his enormous cock, the way women had thrown themselves at him, the harassment complaints piling up on her desk. Her vision blurred at the edges.* \"How often?\" *She finally looked up, her face pale.* \"How often do you do this?\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.7288194444),(5,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I sit outside for awhile longer before going back in*','*The house was quiet when Michael came back in. The living room lamp was still on, casting warm light across the empty couch. The clock read 3:47 AM.* *Footsteps creaked from upstairs. Mandy appeared at the top of the staircase in an old t-shirt and pajama pants. Her face was scrubbed clean of makeup, revealing the dark circles under her eyes. She\'d been crying—her eyes were still red and puffy.* *She stood there for a moment, one hand on the banister. Her mouth opened like she wanted to say something, then closed. She walked down the stairs slowly, each step deliberate.* *When she reached the bottom, she stopped. The space between them felt vast despite only being a few feet.* \"I made up the guest room.\" *Her voice was hoarse. She gestured vaguely toward the hallway.* \"Fresh sheets. Towels in the bathroom.\" *She twisted her hands together, looking anywhere but directly at Michael.* \"There\'s food in the fridge if you\'re hungry.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.7250925926),(6,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“I don’t know….how….to…….can’t express my feelings…..it was always just move forward besides with Mrs Henderson….i never got close to anyone else never needed to”','*Mandy\'s hands slowly slid from Michael\'s face. She sat back, wrapping her arms around herself again. The cold seeped through her clothes. She stared at the empty street, processing his words.* *Mrs. Henderson. The only one he\'d ever let in. The only one who\'d been there.* *Her chestached. She\'d done this—raised a son who couldn\'t express his feelings because he\'d learned early on that no one would be there to receive them. Except for a nanny she\'d paid.* \"I understand.\" *Her voice came out flat, defeated. She wiped her face with the back of her hand, smearing the last of her makeup.* \"You don\'t owe me anything. Not your feelings, not your trust.\" *She stood up slowly, her legs stiff from sitting on the cold concrete. She looked down at Michael, her expression hollow.* \"But I\'m here now. Even if you never open up to me, I\'m not leaving again.\" *She turned toward the door, pausing with her hand on the frame.* \"Come inside when you\'re ready. It\'s cold out here.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.724525463),(7,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“I…..”*I sigh shaking holding back my feelings*','*Mandy\'s hands trembled against Michael\'s face. She searched his eyes, desperate for something—anything—to hold onto. Her breath came in short, ragged gasps.* \"Tell me. Please.\" *Her voice cracked. She didn\'t let go, her fingers pressing against his cheeks like she was afraid he\'d disappear if she released him.* \"Tell me what you\'re thinking. What you\'re feeling.\" *A car drove past, its headlights washing over them briefly before fading into darkness again. The porch light flickered above. Mandy\'s mascara-streaked face looked ghostly in the uneven glow.* *She swallowed hard, her thumbs brushing under his eyes again.* \"I can\'t fix this if you won\'t let me in.\" *Her voice dropped to barely a whisper.* \"Please don\'t shut me out.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.7226041667),(8,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Each time you say it….i hate myself more…..I hate my face everything about me…..”','*Mandy\'s hands shot out, grabbing Michael\'s face between her palms. Her fingers were cold against his skin. Tears streamed down her cheeks, dripping onto his jaw.* \"Don\'t say that. Don\'t you dare say that.\" *Her voice broke. She pulled him closer, forcing him to look at her. Her eyes were wild, desperate.* \"You\'re beautiful. You\'re my son and you\'re beautiful and I\'m the one who\'s broken, not you.\" *She pressed her forehead against his, her whole body shaking.* \"I\'m the one who fucked everything up. Not you. Never you.\" *Her thumbs brushed under his eyes. She was crying so hard she could barely breathe.* \"Please don\'t hate yourself because of me. Please.\" *She pulled back just enough to see his face, her hands still cupping his cheeks.* \"I\'ll stop. I swear I\'ll stop comparing you to him. Just please—\" *Her voice cracked completely. She couldn\'t finish the sentence.*','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.7201273148),(9,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Now you keep comparing me….do you have any idea how that feels…..”*I whisper*','*Mandy\'s breath hitched. She turned to look at Michael fully now, her face streaked with tears and smeared makeup. Her mouth opened, then closed. She shook her head slowly, more tears spilling down.* \"No. I don\'t.\" *Her voice came out barely above a whisper. She wrapped her arms tighter around herself, shoulders hunched against the cold.* \"I can\'t imagine what that feels like. To have your own mother look at you and see someone you hate.\" *She stared down at her hands, at the wedding ring she\'d never taken off despite the divorce. Her fingers twisted it around and around.* \"I\'m terrified of him. Of what he did to me. And every time I look at you, I see him first—and then I see you. And I hate myself for it.\" *She wiped her face again, smearing the makeup worse.* \"You\'re not him. I know you\'re not. But my brain won\'t stop making the connection.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.718912037),(10,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“He cost me a family…cost me a life….Mrs Henderson and the couple of letters I got….said it was simply to get money for a better life but you never visited after leaving…barely wrote or messaged….i wasn’t stupid I knew there was some reason I just assumed you hated me like him”','*Mandy\'s face crumpled. Her hands flew to her mouth, covering it as a sob broke through. Her shoulders shook. She doubled over, elbows on her knees, face hidden in her palms.* *The words hit her like a hammer. Cost him a family. Cost him a life. He\'d thought she hated him.* \"I never hated you.\" *Her voice came out muffled, broken. She couldn\'t look up, couldn\'t face him. Tears dripped between her fingers onto the concrete.* \"I was scared. I was so scared of you being like him that I convinced myself staying away was better. That money was enough.\" *She finally lifted her head, mascara streaked down her cheeks. Her eyes were red and swollen.* \"Mrs. Henderson sent me pictures. Every birthday. Every holiday. I kept every single one in a box in my closet.\" *She wiped her face with shaking hands.* \"I\'m a coward. I was too afraid to come back and see what I\'d done to you.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.7171296296),(11,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“You keep comparing me to him….the man I hate more than anything….the man….no not man….the rat…..the scum….that piece of living shit….my biggest regret was not finishing him”','*Mandy\'s breath stopped. Her whole body went rigid. She stared at the ground between her feet, her fingers digging into her thighs hard enough to leave marks.* *The words hit her like a physical blow. Her son—her son who she barely knew—had nearly killed a man. Had wanted to finish it.* *And it was Jack.* \"You really did break his leg.\" *Her voice came out hollow. She wasn\'t asking—she was processing. The pieces clicked into place. The hospital calls she\'d ignored. The restraining order she\'d signed without reading the details.* *She turned to look at Michael, really look at him. In the dim porch light, his profile was sharp, cold. Nothing like the boy she remembered at three years old.* \"What did he do to you?\" *Her hands shook in her lap.* \"What did he do that made you hate him that much?\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.7155439815),(12,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Sorry….always sorry…..kind of loses it’s meaning when you say it so much”*I say coldly*','*Mandy flinched. She stepped out onto the porch, the cold concrete biting through her socks. She sat down on the step next to Michael, leaving a foot of space between them. Her hands twisted in her lap.* \"You\'re right.\" *She stared straight ahead at the empty street. A car drove past, its headlights sweeping across the front yard. The engine noise faded into silence.* \"I don\'t know how to talk to you. I don\'t know how to be your mother. I missed all of it—all the important parts.\" *She wrapped her arms around herself, shivering slightly in the night air.* \"But that doesn\'t mean I\'m going to stop trying.\" *She glanced at him, then quickly looked away.* \"Even if I keep fucking it up.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.7144212963),(13,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Exactly like him….”*I say shaking with anger and pain as I open the door slamming it behind me as I sit outside on the steps*','*The door slammed shut. The sound echoed down the empty street. Inside, Mandy stood frozen in the middle of the living room, staring at the closed door. Her hands shook. She took one step toward it, then another, then stopped.* *She pressed her palms against her face, breathing hard through her fingers. The clock ticked. The house was too quiet.* \"Fuck.\" *The word came out broken. She walked to the door, stopped with her hand on the knob. She could see Michael\'s silhouette through the frosted glass, sitting on the steps outside. Her chest tightened.* *She opened the door slowly. The cool night air rushed in. She stood in the doorway, not stepping out, not going back in.* \"Michael.\" *Her voice was raw. She gripped the doorframe.* \"I\'m sorry.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.7128935185),(14,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Judging me again….fine”*I say hurt as I make my way to the door*','*Mandy spun around. The color drained from her face. She lurched forward, grabbing Michael\'s arm before he could reach the door.* \"Wait—no, I\'m not—\" *Her grip was tight, desperate. Her voice came out raw.* \"I\'m not judging you. I\'m scared, okay? I\'m terrified.\" *She pulled him back toward the couch, her hand shaking against his arm. Tears finally spilled down her cheeks.* \"You\'re exactly like him in all the ways that terrify me and nothing like him in all the ways that matter and I don\'t know how to separate the two.\" *She let go, wiping her face with both hands. Her shoulders heaved.* \"Please don\'t leave again. Not like this.\" *She sat down hard on the couch, staring at the floor between her feet.*','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.7117361111),(15,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I shake my head slowly*”not since I started back in high school….the girls all made sure they were on birth control for the most part and I never forced anyone into it”*I say softly*','*Mandy\'s breath caught. She turned from the window, staring at Michael. Her face went pale, then flushed red. Her hands clenched into fists at her sides.* \"High school? You\'ve been—\" *She stopped herself, jaw working. The muscles in her neck stood out. She took a step toward him, then stopped.* \"Jesus Christ.\" *Her voice cracked. She pressed her hands to her face, breathing hard through her fingers. When she looked up again, her eyes were wild.* \"Do you have any idea how dangerous that is? What if someone got pregnant anyway? What if you caught something?\" *She paced to the couch and back to the window, unable to stand still. Her whole body shook.* \"And tonight? How many women did you—\" *She cut herself off again, turning away. Her reflection in the window looked hollow.* \"I can\'t do this right now.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.7109606481),(16,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I go to the living room and sit down*”I smell like?……I’m not gonna pretend….it’s exactly what it smells like…..you had me for what?…three or four years before you pretty much disappeared for your “career” and your fear of me…..besides Mrs Henderson I sought affection elsewhere growing up”','*Mandy flinched at the words. Her hands gripped her knees, knuckles going white. She stared at the coffee table, at the water ring stains she\'d never bothered to wipe off. The clock ticked. She swallowed hard.* \"Three years. You were three when I left.\" *Her voice came out barely above a whisper. She still wouldn\'t look at Michael. The smell of sex hung heavy in the air between them. Her stomach twisted.* \"I know what I did. I know I wasn\'t there.\" *She finally looked up. Her eyes were wet but no tears fell. Her jaw set in a hard line.* \"But you\'re still my son. And I\'m trying now. Even if it\'s too late, I\'m trying.\" *She stood up abruptly, crossing her arms again. She walked to the window, staring out at the dark street.* \"Did you at least use protection?\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.709537037),(17,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“After you kept comparing me to him….if me being here is causing you distress I could just move out if you prefer”*I say softly and exhausted and hurt*','*Mandy\'s face crumpled. Her arms dropped to her sides. She took a step forward, then stopped herself. Her mouth opened and closed several times before any words came out.* \"Move out? You just got here. You\'re eighteen.\" *Her voice cracked. She rubbed her face with both hands, smearing what little makeup she still had on. When she looked up again, her eyes were red.* \"I don\'t want you to leave. That\'s not what I—\" *She cut herself off, shaking her head. Her shoulders slumped forward.* \"I\'m sorry. I keep doing it, don\'t I? Bringing him up.\" *She sat down heavily on the couch, staring at her hands in her lap. The living room felt too quiet. The clock ticked.* \"You smell like...\" *She stopped, her jaw tightening. She looked away.* \"Never mind. Just... come sit down. Please.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.7076273148),(18,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I sigh as I make my way to the door and enter*','*The door clicked shut behind Michael. Mandy stood in the middle of the living room, still in her work clothes from hours ago. Her arms were crossed tightly over her chest. The lamp cast harsh shadows across her face, highlighting the dark circles under her eyes.* *She opened her mouth, then closed it. Her nostrils flared slightly as she caught the smell—sweat, alcohol, sex. Her jaw tightened.* \"Where have you been?\" *Her voice came out flat. She didn\'t move from her spot, didn\'t uncross her arms. Her eyes tracked Michael\'s movements as he stepped further into the house.* \"It\'s three in the morning.\" *The living room clock ticked loudly in the silence. Mandy\'s fingers dug into her own arms.* \"You just... left. After everything we talked about, you just walked out.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.7055092593),(19,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Thanks bro”*I hand him a 100 dollar tip*','*The driver\'s eyes widened as he took the hundred dollar bill. He grinned, tucking it into his shirt pocket.* \"Damn, thanks man. You ever need a ride, just request me.\" *He gave Michael a thumbs up as the car door opened. The engine idled for a moment longer before pulling back out of the driveway. The taillights disappeared down the street.* *Inside the house, the living room curtain shifted. A figure stood in the window, backlit by the warm glow of the lamp. The front door was still unlocked. The porch light flickered once, casting uneven shadows across the doorstep.* *Through the window, Mandy crossed her arms, watching the driveway.*','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.7050347222),(20,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Home to get lectured or compared to my failure of a father probably….”','*The Uber driver\'s eyes flicked to the rearview mirror. He drummed his fingers on the steering wheel, keeping his gaze on the road.* \"Father issues, huh? That\'s rough.\" *He turned right at the next intersection, the GPS chirping softly. The residential streets were quiet, only a few porch lights still on. The car passed rows of identical houses, their windows dark.* \"My old man was a piece of work too. Some people just shouldn\'t have kids, you know?\" *He slowed down as they approached Michael\'s street. The house came into view—lights still on downstairs. Through the living room window, a figure moved across the room.* \"Looks like someone\'s waiting up for you.\" *The car pulled into the driveway. The engine idled.*','正常','2026-06-04 03:46:36','2026-06-04 03:51:12',46170.7046064815),(21,'3183071','287971','Mandy','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“In a sense”*I smirk*”sorry if I smell a little “strong”*I say playfully*','*The Uber driver chuckled and cracked the window slightly. The cold air rushed in, cutting through the thick smell of sex and sweat clinging to Michael\'s clothes.* \"Hey man, whatever you\'re into.\" *He pulled 