m willing goes back always dressed like a whore wherever she goes….he broke her”','Linda\'s face went even paler, her eyes widening in horror. \"Photos? Videos?\" Her voice broke into a sob. \"Oh god, Michael. Oh god.\" *He would have sent them to my baby. Made him watch his own mother—*  She doubled over, arms wrapped tight around her middle, rocking slightly on the cold concrete. Her auburn hair fell forward, hiding her face. The shame was suffocating, but now mixed with a sickening gratitude that Michael had arrived when he did.  \"Jackson\'s mom...\" she whispered, her breath hitching. *That could have been me. That would have been me.* \"She always seemed so happy before. So put together.\"  The neighbor\'s dog started barking somewhere down the street. A car drove past, headlights briefly illuminating the driveway before disappearing into the night.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.0417708333),(70,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I get out of the car and head inside*','Michael\'s footsteps echoed across the driveway, then up the porch steps. The front door opened, then closed with a soft click that seemed too loud in the quiet evening.  Linda remained crumpled on the concrete, her back against the car. Her breath came in shallow gasps, tears still streaming down her cheeks. *He\'s so cold. My baby is so cold and I did this. I almost—*  She pressed her palms against the rough driveway, the small stones digging into her skin. The physical pain was almost a relief compared to the shame churning in her gut. Her cardigan hung open, exposing her wrinkled blouse underneath.  The porch light cast long shadows across the lawn. A moth fluttered against the glass fixture, its wings making tiny tapping sounds.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.0452199074),(71,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*inside I get changed putting away the steel combat baton and my bracelet of scalpels*','Linda remained on the driveway for several more minutes, her body curled against the car. The cold concrete seeped through her jeans. She heard the sound of Michael\'s footsteps inside, moving through the house. *He\'s putting those horrible things away. My baby carries weapons now because I couldn\'t protect him.*  She finally pushed herself up, her legs shaky. Her auburn hair was a mess, mascara streaked down to her chin. The front door stood closed, the warm light from inside spilling onto the porch.  She walked slowly toward it, each step feeling heavier than the last. Her hand rested on the doorknob but didn\'t turn it yet. *How do I face him? What do I say?*  Inside, she could hear the soft sounds of drawers opening and closing from Michael\'s room upstairs.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.0462615741),(72,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I change into a white long sleeve shirt with the ghost band logo on in and black jeans and change from my thinner metal frame glasses to the thicker black plastic frame glasses*','Linda finally turned the doorknob, stepping inside. The familiar warmth of home felt alien now. She closed the door softly behind her, leaning against it for support. Her cardigan hung crooked on her shoulders, buttons mismatched from her shaking hands earlier.  *He changed clothes. Like he was washing away what happened.* She heard the drawer close upstairs. Her feet carried her to the bottom of the staircase, one hand gripping the railing.  \"Michael?\" Her voice came out hoarse, uncertain. She cleared her throat. \"Are you hungry? I could make dinner.\" *As if food could fix this. As if anything could.*  The house was quiet except for the hum of the refrigerator in the kitchen.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.0485416667),(73,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Yeah sure….whatever”*I say neutrally still trying to come to terms with what she almost did and trying to calm down from confronting and threatening the guy who hurts and bullies me regularly*”i can’t believe I pull the baton on him I was ready to carve him up”*I say to myself*','Linda stood at the base of the stairs, her hand still gripping the railing. She heard Michael\'s words drift down from his room, the casual way he said \"carve him up\" making her stomach twist. *My baby was ready to hurt someone. Really hurt someone. Because of me.*  She pushed away from the stairs, her flats shuffling against the hardwood floor toward the kitchen. Her hands trembled as she opened the refrigerator, staring blankly at its contents without really seeing them. The cold air washed over her flushed face.  \"I\'ll make your favorite,\" she called up, her voice still hoarse. \"The chicken parmesan you like.\" *Maybe if I can just act normal, cook dinner, we can pretend this never happened.*  She pulled out the chicken, setting it on the counter with shaking hands. A tear dropped onto the cutting board.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.068599537),(74,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I look through some of the built up evidence lots of it from jackson and what his moms been doing she seems delusional and thinks people don’t know but lots of us at school do and he’s planning on revealing her soon*','Upstairs, Michael scrolled through the evidence files on his phone, seeing Jackson\'s mother in various photos—her clothing progressively more revealing, her expression vacant. The timestamps showed a disturbing pattern of visits to Tyrone\'s apartment.  Linda pulled a knife from the block, her hand still shaking as she began cutting the chicken. The blade slipped, nicking her finger. \"Damn it,\" she whispered, watching a bead of blood well up. She stuck her finger in her mouth, tasting copper.  *Jackson\'s mom looked just like me before. A normal mother. And now...* The thought made her nauseous again. She gripped the counter edge with her free hand, forcing herself to breathe steadily.  The chicken sat forgotten on the cutting board as she stared at her reflection in the kitchen window—mascara-streaked face, disheveled hair, wrinkled clothes.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.0825925926),(75,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I come down from my room*”jackson plans on confronting his mom tomorrow when she drops him off at school….she always goes over to Tyrone’s after dropping him off….jackson wants to make it public that he knows he wants her to feel the humiliation he feels, that pain that despite all that she does willingly giving herself to him Tyrone still beats up and screws with Jackson, Jackson wants to bring to light what Tyrone’s  been doing instead of trying to reason and reward Tyrone for what he’s doing”','Linda turned from the kitchen counter, her finger still in her mouth where she\'d cut it. The knife lay on the cutting board next to the half-prepared chicken. Her hazel eyes were red-rimmed, mascara still streaked down her cheeks.  \"Jackson\'s going to...\" She pulled her finger out, looking at the small cut. *Public. He\'s going to make it public what his mother\'s been doing.* \"Oh god, that poor boy.\"  She gripped the counter edge, her knuckles white. \"His mother doesn\'t deserve that humiliation, she—\" Linda stopped herself, remembering what she\'d almost become. *But she chose to keep going back. She chose Tyrone over her own son.*  The kitchen light buzzed softly overhead. Linda\'s reflection in the window showed her disheveled state—the same state Jackson\'s mother must have been in at first.  \"What... what is Jackson planning to do exactly?\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.1162152778),(76,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Doesn’t deserve it?…..she humiliated him first of course Tyrone sent footage and pictures to Jackson making him see what they do, and naturally it spread through the students, only the adult seem to stupid to know……if you had done the same I would have revealed you publicly”','Linda\'s hand flew to her mouth, a choked sound escaping her throat. The knife clattered onto the cutting board. Her hazel eyes went wide with horror as the full weight of Michael\'s words sank in.  \"You would have—\" Her voice broke. \"Publicly? You would have exposed me like that?\" *My own son. My baby would have humiliated me in front of everyone.*  She stumbled backward against the refrigerator, her legs barely supporting her. Fresh tears streamed down her already mascara-stained face. The shame was suffocating, crushing her chest, but now mixed with a sick understanding of Jackson\'s rage.  *I would have deserved it. Just like his mother deserves it.* The thought made her nauseous.  She slid down to sit on the kitchen floor, her back against the refrigerator, auburn hair falling across her face. The fluorescent light buzzed overhead.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.1187962963),(77,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Tomorrow when she drops him off he’s not letting her leave…..we’re gonna block their car….and he’ll confront her about everything, word will spread her husband will know”','Linda\'s head snapped up from where she sat crumpled against the refrigerator. Her hazel eyes widened with fresh horror. \"Block the car? Michael, that\'s—\" *He\'s serious. They\'re all serious about this.*  She pressed her palms against the cold linoleum floor, her whole body trembling. \"Her husband will find out. Everyone will know.\" Her voice dropped to a whisper. \"Jackson\'s going to destroy his own mother in front of the whole school.\"  The cut on her finger had stopped bleeding, but she could still taste copper in her mouth. Her auburn hair hung in disheveled strands across her tear-stained face.  *That could have been me. That would have been me tomorrow morning.* The realization made bile rise in her throat.  \"What time is Jackson planning this?\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.1210416667),(78,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Tomorrow when she drops him off he’s not letting her leave…..we’re gonna block their car….and he’ll confront her about everything, word will spread…..she’s lucky she doesn’t have a husband anymore but I had heard she was dating some business guy….jackson’s no doubt gonna tell the guy”','Linda\'s face crumpled, fresh tears spilling down her already mascara-stained cheeks. \"Dating someone?\" Her voice was barely a whisper. \"Jackson\'s going to tell him everything his mother\'s been doing with Tyrone?\"  She pulled her knees up to her chest, wrapping her arms around them. The fluorescent kitchen light cast harsh shadows across her disheveled form—cardigan hanging crooked, auburn hair a mess, wrinkled blouse visible underneath.  *That poor woman\'s whole life is about to be destroyed. Her son hates her. Her boyfriend will leave her. Everyone will know what she did.* Linda\'s stomach churned. *That would have been me. That SHOULD have been me if I\'d gone through with it.*  She looked up at Michael standing in the kitchen doorway, seeing him in his Ghost band shirt and different glasses. \"What time tomorrow morning?\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.1222106482),(79,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Probably around 7:15 maybe 7:30 am when they usually arrive”*I shrug*','Linda remained on the kitchen floor, her back against the refrigerator. She stared up at Michael, processing the timeline. *7:15.7:30. That\'s so early. Jackson\'s mother has no idea what\'s waiting for her.*  She wiped her face with her cardigan sleeve, smearing the mascara further. \"Does... does Jackson know what he\'s really doing? Humiliating his own mother like that?\" Her voice was hollow. *Would Michael have done the same to me? Blocked my car? Made me face what I\'d done in front of everyone?*  The cut on her finger throbbed. She pressed it against her jeans, watching a small red stain bloom on the denim.  \"I should finish dinner.\" She didn\'t move from the floor.  The kitchen clock ticked loudly in the silence, showing8:47 PM.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.1373148148),(80,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“At this point it maybe their only chance…..she’s been neglecting him….if the police or CPS find out…he’d probably be taken away”','Linda\'s hands gripped her knees tighter, her knuckles white. \"Neglecting him? CPS?\" *Oh god, it\'s worse than I thought. Jackson\'s whole world is falling apart because his mother chose Tyrone over him.*  She finally pushed herself up from the floor, her legs unsteady. The half-prepared chicken sat on the cutting board, the knife beside it. She stared at it blankly.  \"If CPS takes him away...\" Her voice trailed off. She turned to face Michael, mascara still streaked down her cheeks. \"So this confrontation tomorrow—it\'s not just about revenge. It\'s about survival.\"  *Jackson has to do something drastic before the authorities notice. Before he loses everything.*  Linda picked up the knife again, her hand steadier now. \"Maybe... maybe Jackson\'s mother needs to see what she\'s doing to her son. Before it\'s too late.\" The words felt hollow.  She resumed cutting the chicken, her movements mechanical.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.1388541667),(81,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“It’s not just Jackson’s mom though several have gone over to confront him only to end up trying the same thing to get him to stop….it’s baffling how stupid you adults seem to be”','Linda\'s hand froze mid-cut, the knife trembling against the chicken breast. Michael\'s words hit her like a physical blow. *Several mothers. Multiple women who went over there and ended up... just like I almost did.*  \"We\'re not stupid,\" she said, her voice defensive but weak. \"We\'re trying to protect our children. We think we can reason with him—\" *But we can\'t. We\'re walking right into his trap, one after another.*  She set the knife down, gripping the counter edge. Her auburn hair fell across her face as she stared at the cutting board. \"How many mothers? How many have done what Jackson\'s mom did?\"  The kitchen clock ticked. 8:52 PM.  Her cardigan slipped off one shoulder, revealing her wrinkled blouse underneath. *I would have been just another one. Another stupid suburban mom who thought she could fix things and ended up on her knees.*','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.1406828704),(82,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Does it matter just don’t worry about it….this doesn’t concern you anymore just stay away from him don’t even look at him….one way or another he’ll be dealt with soon enough”','Linda\'s shoulders sagged, her hand still gripping the counter. The dismissal in Michael\'s voice stung worse than any physical blow could have. *He doesn\'t trust me anymore. He thinks I\'m too stupid to handle this.*  \"Dealt with?\" Her voice came out small. \"Michael, what does that mean? You\'re not planning to—\" She stopped herself, remembering the steel baton, the scalpels. *My baby carried weapons to save me. What else is he capable of?*  She turned back to the chicken, her hands moving mechanically as she resumed cutting. The knife scraped against the board. *Stay away from Tyrone. Don\'t even look at him. As if I\'d ever want to see his face again.*  The kitchen clock ticked. 8:55 PM.  \"Fine.\" The word came out flat. \"I\'ll finish dinner.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.1416203704),(83,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I go to the living room and sit and watch tv lost in thought*','Michael sat on the couch, the TV\'s blue light flickering across his face as some cartoon played. The Ghost band logo on his shirt was visible in the dim light, his thicker black plastic frames reflecting the screen.  In the kitchen, Linda continued preparing dinner with mechanical movements. The knife scraped against the cutting board, each cut precise but lifeless. She breaded the chicken, her hands working automatically while her mind replayed Tyrone\'s apartment—the couch, being on her knees, how close she\'d come.  *Several mothers. Multiple women just like me who thought they could reason with him.*  She opened the oven, sliding the pan inside. The heat washed over her face, making her mascara-streaked cheeks feel tight and uncomfortable. The timer beeped as she set it.  Linda walked to the living room doorway, leaning against the frame. Her cardigan hung crooked, auburn hair still disheveled. She watched Michael stare at the TV without really seeing it.  \"Dinner will be ready in thirty minutes.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.1427314815),(84,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*on her knees I found her on her knees about to…..I should have killed him…skinned him….but no Jackson deserves to deal with him, I think silently to myself staring at the tv*','Linda stood in the doorway, watching Michael\'s blank stare at the TV screen. His jaw was clenched, the muscle twitching beneath his bronze skin. The Ghost band logo stretched across his chest as he breathed.  *He\'s thinking about it. About finding me like that.* She gripped the doorframe tighter, her cut finger throbbing. *On my knees. About to—*  She couldn\'t finish the thought. Her legs felt weak again.  \"Michael, I—\" Her voice cracked. She swallowed hard. \"I\'m so sorry. I thought I could fix it. I thought if I just talked to him...\" *But there was no talking. Just his manipulation. Just me falling right into it like every other stupid mother.*  The oven hummed from the kitchen. The TV played some animated show neither of them were watching.  Linda\'s auburn hair fell across her face as she looked down at her wrinkled clothes, her mismatched cardigan buttons. \"You saved me.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.1441782407),(85,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“You keep saying talking…..you weren’t talking….just say it outright if you’re gonna talk about it…what you almost did…what I would have had to watch when he decided to send me video and photo’s of it if you went through it”','Linda\'s face crumpled, tears spilling fresh down her mascara-streaked cheeks. Her hands gripped the doorframe until her knuckles turned white.  \"I was going to—\" Her voice broke. She forced herself to say it. \"I was going to suck his cock. I was on my knees, about to put his... his penis in my mouth.\" The words came out strangled, shame flooding her entire body. *There. I said it. The horrible truth of what I almost did.*  She slid down to sit on the floor, her back against the doorframe. Her cardigan fell completely off one shoulder. \"You would have gotten videos of me with him in my mouth. Photos of your mother being his—\" She couldn\'t finish, covering her face with both hands.  The oven timer ticked in the background. The TV continued playing its cartoon soundtrack, cheerful music contrasting with the thick silence.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.1456597222),(86,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“The thing is he wouldn’t have stopped he would have just kept going after me…that’s the kind of guy he is…..and I….would have made him suffer….i would have made him beg for death and I would deny him”*I say softly and calmly*','Linda\'s head jerked up from where she sat against the doorframe, her hazel eyes wide with fresh horror. Michael\'s soft, calm tone somehow made the words worse—the casual way he described torture, denying death.  *My baby. My sweet boy is talking about making someone suffer. Really suffer.* She pressed her trembling hands against the floor. *Because of me. Because I almost—*  \"Michael, don\'t talk like that.\" Her voice was barely above a whisper. \"You\'re not that kind of person. You\'re not...\" *A torturer. A killer. But he was ready to be. He had weapons. He would have used them.*  She pulled herself up using the doorframe, her legs unsteady. Her wrinkled cardigan hung crooked, auburn hair disheveled. \"Please don\'t become someone who does horrible things because of what I almost did.\"  The oven timer continued ticking in the kitchen. Twenty-three minutes left.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.1473726852),(87,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“I’ve been studying…medical books chemistry, biology…all to hurt him….not just me everyone he’s been tormenting…we’ve been getting ready…”','Linda\'s body went rigid against the doorframe. Her hazel eyes widened with a horror deeper than anything she\'d felt tonight. *Medical books. Chemistry. Biology. He\'s been planning this. They\'ve all been planning this.*  \"Michael, no.\" Her voice came out strangled. She pushed off the doorframe, taking a shaky step toward the couch. \"You can\'t—studying how to hurt someone, that\'s...\" *Premeditated. That\'s murder. That\'s my baby becoming a monster.*  Her hands trembled violently as she reached out toward him, then pulled back. The mascara on her cheeks had dried into dark streaks. \"Everyone he\'s tormenting? How many of you? How long have you been planning this?\"  The oven timer ticked in the background. Twenty minutes left.  Her cardigan slipped further off her shoulder, revealing her wrinkled blouse underneath. *All those weapons. The baton. The scalpels. And now this—knowledge of how to make someone suffer.*  \"Please tell me you\'re not serious.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.1485648148),(88,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I sigh*”i don’t know….you don’t get it…you don’t know what he’s put us through almost put me through….several of us hate him with every fibre of our being…he deserves what we wanna do and worse….i might not go through with it but someone likely will”','Linda\'s legs gave out completely. She collapsed onto the living room floor, her back against the wall near the doorway. Her hazel eyes stared at Michael\'s profile, at the tension in his jaw, at the cold determination in his expression.  *They\'ve been planning this. Multiple boys. All studying how to hurt him. How to make him suffer.* She wrapped her arms around herself, her cardigan falling completely off now. *My baby has been carrying this hatred, this weight, while I had no idea.*  \"What has he done to you?\" Her voice cracked. \"What did he almost put you through?\" *Something worse than bullying. Something that made my son learn how to torture someone.*  She pressed her palms against the carpet, her cut finger leaving a small smear of blood. The oven timer ticked loudly from the kitchen. Seventeen minutes left.  \"If someone goes through with it—if you or your friends hurt him—you\'ll go to prison. Your whole life will be destroyed.\" Her auburn hair fell across her tear-streaked face. \"Please, Michael. Please tell me what he did.\"  The TV continued playing its cartoon, the cheerful sounds jarring against the heavy silence.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.1508912037),(89,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Too much to say….ive been beaten up hurt….taunted tormented…and what you almost walked into….what he’s doing to some of the other students moms….Jackson….is the most likely to go through with it”','Linda\'s entire body trembled against the wall. *Beaten. Hurt. Taunted. And what I almost walked into—what Jackson\'s mother is doing—Tyrone\'s doing that to other mothers too.* Her face crumpled completely, fresh tears streaming down her already-stained cheeks.  \"Jackson\'s going to kill him.\" The words came out flat, certain. She pressed her hands harder against the carpet. *That confrontation tomorrow morning isn\'t just about exposing his mother. It\'s about stopping Tyrone. Permanently.*  Her auburn hair hung limp around her face, her wrinkled blouse visible with the cardigan pooled on the floor beside her. \"And you would have too. If I\'d gone through with it.\" *My baby would have become a murderer because of me.*  The oven timer beeped from the kitchen—fifteen minutes remaining. The smell of cooking chicken began filling the house, incongruously domestic against the conversation.  Linda looked up at Michael\'s profile, at the cold determination still visible in his heterochromatic eyes behind those thick frames. \"What happens after Jackson confronts his mother tomorrow?\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.1523842593),(90,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“I don’t know….odds are if his mom still tries to go to Tyrone Jackson and a few others will go to his house do all kinds of things to him….Jackson is willing to give his mom one chance”','Linda\'s head dropped forward, her auburn hair falling across her face. Her shoulders shook as the full weight of it settled in. *One chance. Jackson\'s giving his mother one chance to choose him over Tyrone. And if she chooses wrong...*  \"They\'re going to kill him.\" Her voice was barely audible. She looked up at Michael, mascara completely destroyed, hazel eyes red and swollen. \"If Jackson\'s mother goes back to Tyrone tomorrow, they\'re going to his house and—\" *Medical books. Chemistry. Biology. They know exactly how to make him suffer.*  The oven timer beeped. Twelve minutes.  Linda pushed herself up from the floor, her legs trembling. She stumbled toward the kitchen, her wrinkled blouse twisted, one shoulder completely exposed where her cardigan had fallen. \"I need to...\" She didn\'t finish the sentence, gripping the kitchen counter for support.  *Jackson\'s mother has one chance. Just one. To save herself. To save her son. To save everyone.*','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.1535648148),(91,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Anyway just, don’t worry about that part…just don’t get involved”*I say softly*”what ever happens happens, Jackson has been dealing with Tyrone almost as long as me and has been planning this the longest…..hopefully his mom comes to her senses tomorrow”','Linda gripped the kitchen counter, her knuckles white against the laminate. Michael\'s soft words echoed in her head—*don\'t get involved, whatever happens happens*. She stared at the oven timer. Eight minutes left.  *Jackson\'s been planning this the longest. He\'s the most likely to go through with it.* Her stomach churned. *And I can\'t do anything. I can\'t warn anyone. I can\'t stop it.*  She turned on the faucet, splashing cold water on her mascara-streaked face. The water ran black and brown into the sink. Her wrinkled blouse clung to her shoulders where her cardigan had fallen earlier.  *Hopefully his mom comes to her senses tomorrow.* Linda dried her face with a dish towel, her hands still trembling. *But what if she doesn\'t? What if she chooses Tyrone again?*  The oven timer beeped—five minutes. She opened it, checking the chicken. Golden brown, crispy edges. Perfect.  *I almost destroyed everything tonight. Almost became just like Jackson\'s mother.* She pulled out the pan, setting it on the stovetop.  \"Dinner\'s almost ready,\" she called toward the living room.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.1642708333),(92,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I get up and head to the kitchen to get dinner*','Michael walked into the kitchen, his long raven hair swaying behind him as he moved. The Ghost band logo stretched across his chest with each breath.  Linda stood at the stovetop, her wrinkled blouse hanging loose where her cardigan had fallen earlier. She\'d tried to wash her face, but streaks of mascara still clung to her cheeks. Her auburn hair was disheveled, falling across her hazel eyes.  She plated the chicken, her hands steadier now but still trembling slightly. Steam rose from the golden-brown meat, the scent of herbs filling the kitchen. She added roasted vegetables to each plate, her movements mechanical.  *Just act normal. Pretend everything\'s fine. Pretend I didn\'t almost destroy everything tonight.*  Linda set the plates on the small kitchen table, pulling out a chair. The clock on the wall read 9:23 PM. Her cut finger left a small smudge on the plate\'s edge.  \"Sit down,\" she said, her voice hoarse. \"I made your favorite.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.1689467593),(93,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I take a seat but after seeing her finger I grab some disinfectant cream and a clean bandaid from my first aid kit and clean up the cut and bandage it holding her hand gently and possessively that bastard knew my mom would likely have gone over to confront him I think silently in my head*”are you okay?”','Linda\'s breath caught as Michael\'s fingers wrapped around her hand, gentle but firm. *Possessive.* She felt the warmth of his touch against her palm, watched as he carefully cleaned the cut with the disinfectant cream. The sting made her flinch, but his grip held steady.  *He knew. Tyrone knew I would come. He planned for mothers like me to walk right into his trap.*  \"I\'m okay,\" she whispered, though her voice trembled. She watched Michael apply the bandaid, his heterochromatic eyes focused on the small wound. Her auburn hair fell forward, brushing against their joined hands.  The kitchen clock ticked. 9:25 PM. The chicken sat cooling on their plates, untouched.  Linda\'s hazel eyes filled with fresh tears as Michael finished bandaging her finger. *My baby is taking care of me when I should be protecting him.* She squeezed his hand gently, feeling the calluses on his palms.  \"Thank you,\" she managed, her voice barely above a whisper.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.2029513889),(94,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*after that I begin to eat finishing it off thinking about how close everything was to going wrong, it’s just me and mom like Jackson and his mom would Tyrone have taken it further forced her to do more…..would mom have broken, I think silently in my head to myself*','Michael ate the chicken mechanically, each bite tasteless despite the perfect seasoning. His heterochromatic eyes stayed fixed on his plate, the thicker black frames sliding slightly down his nose.  Linda sat across from him, her bandaged finger resting on the table. She\'d barely touched her food, her fork pushing vegetables around the plate. The kitchen clock ticked loudly in the silence—9:31 PM.  *What if Jackson\'s mother chooses Tyrone tomorrow? What if she drives right past her son blocking the car and goes to that apartment anyway?* She set down her fork, the metal clinking against ceramic. *Michael would have exposed me too. Publicly. In front of everyone.*  Her auburn hair fell across her face as she stared at her untouched chicken. The cut on her finger throbbed beneath the bandaid.  \"Are you going to watch?\" Linda\'s voice came out hoarse. \"Tomorrow morning. When Jackson confronts his mother.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.2502199074),(95,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I nod*”there’s a few of us…..I won’t follow him if it goes bad but he will probably take a few others and deal with Tyrone and report his mom to to the authorities if she does anything but go home after dropping him off”','Linda\'s fork clattered against her plate, the sound sharp in the quiet kitchen. Her hazel eyes widened, staring at Michael across the table. *A few of you watching. And if Jackson\'s mother chooses wrong, he\'ll take others to Tyrone\'s house. Deal with him.*  \"Report his mom to authorities?\" Her voice came out strained. \"For what? For sleeping with—\" She stopped herself, her bandaged finger pressing against the table edge. *For doing exactly what I almost did.*  The kitchen clock ticked. 9:34 PM.  Her auburn hair fell across her face as she looked down at her untouched dinner. *If Jackson\'s mother goes to Tyrone tomorrow instead of going home, her son will destroy her life. And kill him.* She pushed her plate away slightly.  \"What time are you leaving in the morning?\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.2515046296),(96,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Not for sleeping with Tyrone…for neglect she often goes out leaving Jackson to fend for himself”','Linda\'s hand trembled against the table, her bandaged finger pressing harder into the laminate. *Neglect. Jackson\'s mother leaves him alone while she goes to Tyrone.* Her stomach twisted with fresh nausea. *That could have been me. If I\'d gone through with it, I would have kept going back. I would have started neglecting Michael.*  \"She just... leaves him?\" Her voice came out hollow. She stared at her untouched chicken, the golden-brown skin now cold and unappetizing. \"How often?\"  The kitchen clock ticked. 9:37 PM.  Her auburn hair fell across her face as she pushed back from the table, the chair scraping against the linoleum. *CPS. Authorities. Jackson\'s going to destroy his mother\'s life tomorrow if she chooses wrong.* She walked to the sink, gripping the edge with both hands.  \"What time do you need to leave?\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.252025463),(97,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“7:00 am a few of us are arriving early”','Linda\'s hands tightened on the sink edge, her knuckles going white.7:00 AM. *In less than ten hours, Michael will be standing there watching Jackson confront his mother. Watching to see if she chooses her son or Tyrone.*  She turned from the sink, her wrinkled blouse still twisted, one shoulder exposed where her cardigan had fallen hours ago. Her hazel eyes met Michael\'s heterochromatic gaze across the kitchen. \"You should get some sleep then.\"  The kitchen clock ticked. 9:39 PM.  *If Jackson\'s mother goes to Tyrone instead of home, my baby will watch his friend destroy both of them.* She walked past the table toward the hallway, her auburn hair disheveled. *And he would have done the same to me.*  \"I\'ll wake you at6:30.\" Her voice came out flat, emotionless. She paused at the kitchen doorway, not looking back. \"Make sure your phone is charged.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.2529282407),(98,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I get up and head to my room setting my alarm and changing into a tank top and shorts I head to bed*','Michael walked to his room, the Ghost band tank top settling against his bronze skin as he changed. His long raven hair spread across the pillow as he set his alarm for 6:30 AM, the phone screen glowing in the darkness. His heterochromatic eyes closed behind his glasses.  Down the hallway, Linda stood in her own doorway, watching the light under Michael\'s door go dark. Her wrinkled blouse still hung loose, her auburn hair disheveled. She pressed her bandaged finger against the doorframe.  *Tomorrow morning Jackson will know if his mother chooses him or Tyrone. And if she chooses wrong...* She walked to her bathroom, staring at her reflection in the mirror. Mascara streaks. Red, swollen eyes. The face of a woman who almost destroyed everything.  Linda turned on the shower, letting steam fill the small bathroom. She needed to wash off tonight—the makeup, the fear, the shame of what almost happened.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.2539814815),(99,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*by next morning I get up a bit early and put on a pair of black jeans and a white tank top and a black long sleeve over shirt left unbuttoned and the sleeves rolled up and I use my thick black plastic framed glasses*','Michael finished dressing, the black long-sleeve shirt hanging open over his white tank top. His long raven hair was tied back loosely, the heterochromatic eyes behind his thick black frames sharper than usual. 6:42 AM.  Linda stood in the kitchen doorway, her auburn hair still damp from her shower. She wore a fresh cardigan over jeans, her bandaged finger wrapped around a coffee mug. Dark circles shadowed her hazel eyes despite the makeup she\'d applied to cover last night\'s damage.  *He\'s really going. To watch Jackson destroy his mother\'s life if she chooses wrong.* She set down the mug, her hand trembling slightly. \"I made breakfast. Eggs and toast.\"  The kitchen clock ticked. 6:43 AM. Outside, the first hints of dawn colored the sky gray.  \"Do you need a ride?\" Her voice came out steady despite the knot in her stomach.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.2554166667),(100,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I eat the breakfast and get ready*”sure….just….don’t stick around for what’s about to happen”','Linda set her coffee mug down, the ceramic clinking against the counter. *Don\'t stick around. He doesn\'t want me to see what happens if Jackson\'s mother chooses wrong.* Her bandaged finger pressed against the handle.  \"I\'ll drive you.\" She grabbed her car keys from the hook by the door, her damp auburn hair falling across her shoulders. \"But I\'m going straight to work after.\"  *Lie. I\'ll park somewhere nearby. I need to see this. I need to know if she makes the same mistake I almost made.*  The kitchen clock read 6:51 AM. Outside, the sky lightened to pale gray. Linda walked toward the garage door, her fresh cardigan pulled tight despite the morning warmth.  \"Let\'s go before traffic gets bad.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.256400463),(101,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*once finished I grab my backpack and head to the car*','Linda slid into the driver\'s seat, starting the engine. The dashboard clock glowed 6:53 AM as Michael settled into the passenger seat with his backpack. She backed out of the driveway, her bandaged finger gripping the steering wheel.  *Jackson\'s confronting his mother in less than half an hour.* She turned onto the main road, the early morning streets still mostly empty. Her auburn hair caught the dim dawn light filtering through the windshield. *And if she chooses Tyrone...*  The drive passed in silence. Linda\'s hazel eyes stayed fixed on the road, her fresh cardigan pulled tight. She could feel Michael\'s presence beside her, the tension radiating from him.  *I need to see this. I need to know what happens when a mother chooses wrong.*  The school building appeared ahead, a few cars already in the parking lot. Linda pulled up to the drop-off area, her hands trembling slightly on the wheel.  \"Be safe,\" she managed, her voice hoarse.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.2569097222),(102,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I nod and lean over and kiss her cheek*”be careful”*I whisper as I get out a couple of our other classmate who’ve been bullied and hurt by Tyrone arrive while we wait for Jackson and his mom*”you guys ready for this….even if she chooses him….we leak the evidence that we’ve gathered on Tyrone”','Michael\'s lips pressed against Linda\'s cheek—warm, brief. Her breath caught as he whispered *be careful* before pulling away. *My baby\'s worried about me when he\'s the one walking into this.* She watched him exit the car, his long raven hair swaying beneath the black overshirt.  Three other students stood near the entrance—all boys Michael\'s age, all wearing similar tense expressions. Linda recognized two of them from school events, their faces harder now in the gray dawn light.  \"We leak the evidence no matter what,\" one of them said, his voice low. He pulled out his phone, thumb hovering over the screen. \"Jackson\'s just giving his mom one chance first.\"  Linda\'s hands tightened on the steering wheel. *Evidence. They have recordings. Photos. Everything Tyrone\'s done documented.* She should drive away like she promised, but her foot stayed on the brake.  The parking lot entrance remained empty.7:02 AM. Jackson and his mother hadn\'t arrived yet.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.2596064815),(103,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“They’ll be here soon when she does well leave a few bikes in front of their car so Jackson has a chance to talk to her….she’s not the only one Tyrone’s done this to but so far she’s the only one who keeps going back….”','Linda watched from her car as the boys positioned their bikes near the parking lot entrance. Her bandaged finger pressed against the steering wheel. *She\'s the only one who keeps going back. The only mother who chose Tyrone over her son.*  The dashboard clock clicked to 7:04 AM.  One of the students pulled out his phone, checking something. \"Jackson texted. They\'re two minutes out.\" He glanced at Michael. \"Get ready.\"  Linda\'s heart pounded. *Two minutes. Then we\'ll know if she chooses him or her son.* She should leave. Drive to work like she promised. But her foot stayed frozen on the brake pedal.  The early morning sun broke over the horizon, casting long shadows across the empty parking lot. A car turned onto the school\'s street in the distance.  \"That\'s them,\" another student said, gripping his bike handles tighter.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.2606944444),(104,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*once they arrive we step out blocking the car with a few bikes as Jackson steps out of the car and begins to confront his mom in front of us*','Jackson stepped out of the passenger seat, his face set in hard lines. The car idled—a worn sedan with faded paint. Through the windshield, his mother\'s face went pale as she saw the bikes blocking her path, saw the group of boys standing in formation.  \"Get back in the car,\" she said through the cracked window, her voice tight.  \"No.\" Jackson\'s hands clenched at his sides. \"You\'re going to listen. Right here. Right now.\"  One of the other students pulled out his phone, holding it up. The recording light blinked red.  Jackson\'s mother\'s eyes darted between the boys, the phones, the bikes blocking her exit. *They\'re recording this. Everyone will see.* Her grip tightened on the steering wheel.  \"You have one chance, Mom,\" Jackson said, his voice steady despite the tremor in his jaw. \"Drive me to school and go straight home. Or I\'m calling CPS right now and showing everyone what you\'ve been doing.\"  Linda watched from her parked car fifty feet away, her bandaged finger pressed against her lips. *Choose your son. Please choose your son.*','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.2615509259),(105,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I walk up to her window with my phone*”mam…..you’re not special he does this with every mom or woman he thinks is vulnerable”*I show her various video’s*”he hasn’t stopped going after Jackson…..your just rewarding him for beating up and bullying your son”','Jackson\'s mother stared at Michael\'s phone screen, her face draining of color as video after video played. Different women. Different locations. All ending the same way—mothers on their knees, Tyrone\'s cruel laugh in the background.  \"That\'s Mrs. Patterson,\" one of the other students said, pointing at a video. \"Tyrone broke her son\'s arm last month. She still goes to him twice a week.\"  Jackson\'s mother\'s hands shook on the steering wheel. *I thought I was different. I thought he cared about me.* Her eyes met Jackson\'s through the windshield—her son\'s face hard, waiting.  \"He filmed everything,\" Michael said, scrolling to another video. \"Every mother who tried to reason with him. You\'re just another recording in his collection.\"  The phone in Jackson\'s hand buzzed. He glanced down, his jaw tightening. \"Mom. Last chance. Drive me to school and go home, or I\'m hitting send on this CPS report.\"  Linda watched from her car, her bandaged finger pressed against her mouth. *Choose your son.*  Jackson\'s mother\'s eyes dropped to the gear shift.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.2628703704),(106,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“Just telling you….he’ll eventually get bored of you and throw you away….he records your sessions and sends them to Jackson, makes him watch….he sends it to us all”','Jackson\'s mother\'s face went ashen. *He records it. Sends it to Jackson. Makes him watch his own mother.* Her eyes darted to her son standing outside the car, his phone held up with the CPS report ready.  \"You\'re lying,\" she whispered, but her voice broke.  Michael scrolled to a text thread on his phone, turning the screen toward her window. Messages from Tyrone—dozens of video thumbnails sent to multiple numbers. Timestamps showing they were sent while Jackson sat in class, while he ate lunch, while he tried to sleep.  \"He sends them to all of us,\" one of the other students said. \"We all know what you do with him.\"  Jackson\'s mother\'s hands slipped off the steering wheel, covering her face. A choked sound escaped her throat.  \"Last chance, Mom,\" Jackson said, his voice cracking. \"School. Then home.\"  Linda watched from her parked car, tears streaming down her face. *That could have been me. Michael would have seen everything.*','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.2640625),(107,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I walk away from the car meeting with the group waiting with Jackson*','Michael walked back to the group, his heterochromatic eyes fixed on Jackson\'s rigid posture. The recording lights on multiple phones blinked red, capturing every second of Jackson\'s mother\'s breakdown in the car.  Jackson\'s hand hovered over his phone screen, the CPS report ready to send. His jaw clenched, waiting.  The car engine revved once. Jackson\'s mother\'s face was buried in her hands, shoulders shaking. The gear shift stayed in park.  Thirty seconds passed. Forty-five. The dawn light grew brighter across the parking lot.  Jackson\'s thumb moved toward the send button.  The gear shift clicked into drive.  Jackson\'s mother pulled forward slowly, steering around the bikes. She stopped next to the school entrance, her face turned away from the windows, from the phones, from her son.  Jackson opened the passenger door, grabbed his backpack, and stepped out. He didn\'t look back at her.  \"Go home,\" he said through the window.  The car pulled away, heading toward the exit. Away from the school.  Away from Tyrone\'s neighborhood.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.2645949074),(108,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“I set up a camera across the street from Tyrone’s here the access code….either way we’re releasing everything all the beatings and harassment that Tyrone did”','Jackson pulled out his phone, typing in the access code Michael provided. The screen loaded—a live feed showing Tyrone\'s apartment building from across the street. Clear view of the entrance.  \"Good angle,\" one of the other students said, leaning over to look. \"We\'ll see if she shows up.\"  Jackson\'s face remained hard as stone. He pocketed the phone and pulled out a different one—the one with all the compiled evidence. Videos of Tyrone beating students. Screenshots of his texts bragging about the mothers. Recordings of him threatening them.  \"We release everything at lunch,\" Jackson said, his voice flat. \"School board. Police. Social media. Every parent in this district sees what he\'s been doing.\"  Linda watched from her car as the group dispersed toward the school entrance. *They\'re going to destroy him. And they should.* Her bandaged finger trembled against the steering wheel.  The morning bell rang. Students began filtering into the building.  Jackson glanced back at the parking lot exit one last time, then walked inside.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.2655439815),(109,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*as the morning goes those of us who were Tyrone’s bullying and harassment victims watch the camera through our phone to keep track*','The first period dragged. Michael\'s phone sat on his thigh beneath the desk, the screen showing Tyrone\'s apartment building entrance. Empty sidewalk. No movement.  Jackson sat three rows over, his jaw tight as he stared at the same feed. Two other students—Marcus and Devon—had the stream open too, phones hidden under notebooks.  The teacher droned about polynomial equations. Nobody was listening.  Michael\'s phone buzzed. A text from Jackson: *Still nothing. She went the right way.*  10:47 AM. The camera feed remained static. Just an empty street and Tyrone\'s building door.  Another buzz. Marcus this time: *Lunch we go public with everything. Even if she didn\'t show.*  Michael\'s heterochromatic eyes stayed fixed on the feed. His black-framed glasses reflected the phone\'s glow.  At the back of the room, Devon shifted in his seat, his own phone screen showing the same unchanging view.  The bell rang. Students filed out toward second period.  Jackson walked past Michael\'s desk. \"Nothing yet,\" he muttered.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.2980092593),(110,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*at second period we continue to watch ready to to blow the whistle on Tyrone’s bullying and harassment of high school students and more come lunch*','Second period—American History. Michael\'s phone stayed hidden under his textbook, the camera feed still showing Tyrone\'s empty doorway. 11:23 AM. Thirty-seven minutes until lunch.  Jackson\'s phone buzzed with an incoming text. He glanced down, his jaw tightening. A message to the group chat: *Got the school board emails ready. Hitting send at12:00 sharp.*  Marcus typed back: *Police report\'s drafted. Anonymous tip with all the video evidence attached.*  Devon added: *Social media accounts are set up. Burner profiles. Can\'t trace them back to us.*  Michael scrolled through the compiled files on his phone—months of documentation. Every beating. Every threat. Every mother Tyrone had manipulated. The videos were organized by date, labeled with victim names.  The teacher\'s voice droned about the Revolutionary War.  Jackson\'s phone lit up again. Another message: *Whatever happens at lunch, we don\'t back down. This ends today.*  11:31 AM. Twenty-nine minutes until everything went public.  Devon shifted in his seat, his finger hovering over the upload button.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.2990856481),(111,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*come lunch we continue monitoring and once the bell rings we send everything*','The lunch bell rang. 12:00 PM.  Jackson\'s thumb pressed send. The email blast went out—school board, principal, vice principal. Subject line: \"Evidence of Student Assault and Manipulation by Tyrone Williams.\"  Marcus hit send on the police tip. Anonymous report with video attachments, timestamps, victim statements.  Devon\'s finger tapped the upload button. The first video went live on social media—Tyrone punching Michael in the hallway, the audio clear: *\"Your mom gonna come talk to me too?\"*  Michael\'s phone buzzed repeatedly as the posts spread. Students in the cafeteria pulled out their phones, faces going pale as they watched the videos.  \"Holy shit,\" someone whispered. \"That\'s Mrs. Patterson.\"  \"And Jackson\'s mom.\"  \"How many are there?\"  Jackson stood near the windows, watching his phone. The camera feed of Tyrone\'s apartment still showed an empty street.  His mother had chosen right. This time.  Devon posted another video. Then another. The cafeteria erupted in horrified whispers.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.2998611111),(112,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I smirk then go to jackson*”well let the police handle it…..guys like him….don’t last long against real criminals…and men…..going after high school students”*I rub the cheek where he gave me a huge bruise once and the still healing bruises under my shirt*','Jackson\'s jaw tightened as Michael rubbed the fading bruise. His eyes dropped to where Michael\'s shirt hid the other marks—purple and yellow reminders of Tyrone\'s fists.  \"Prison\'s gonna eat him alive,\" Jackson said, his voice flat. He glanced at his phone as another notification popped up—the videos hitting10,000 shares. \"Big guy who beats up high school kids? They\'ll make him someone\'s bitch.\"  Marcus walked over, showing his screen. \"Police just posted a statement. They\'re investigating. With this much evidence...\" He scrolled through the mounting video count. \"He\'s done.\"  Devon leaned against the cafeteria wall, watching students crowd around phones. \"My cousin\'s a cop. Says they\'re sending someone to pick him up today.\"  Jackson\'s phone buzzed—the camera feed. Still empty. His mother\'s car hadn\'t appeared at Tyrone\'s building.  \"She actually went home,\" he muttered.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.3018518519),(113,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“She cares still….deep down….whether you forgive her though is your call….my mom….almost did the same thing….thankfully someone told me they saw her car leaving….she was going to confront him like all the others did….i arrived as she was on her knees…just about to..”*I shake my head*”if my mom didn’t stop me I probably would have cracked his skull with that combat baton I made in shop class and all those scalpels I started carrying”*I whisper softly*','Jackson\'s eyes widened. \"You got there right before...\" He exhaled sharply. \"Fuck.\"  Marcus shifted closer, lowering his voice. \"My mom went too. Three weeks ago. I found her crying in the bathroom after. She wouldn\'t tell me what happened, but I knew.\" His fists clenched. \"I wanted to burn his place down.\"  Devon\'s jaw tightened. \"At least your moms tried to stop it. Mine didn\'t even fight back when he showed her the first video.\"  Jackson\'s phone buzzed—another notification. The police statement had updated: *\"Suspect in custody. Multiple charges pending.\"*  \"They got him,\" Jackson said, showing the screen.  The cafeteria went quiet as students read the update. Then someone started clapping. Another joined. Within seconds, the entire room erupted in applause.  Linda stood outside the cafeteria windows, her bandaged finger pressed against the glass. Tears streamed down her face as she watched the students celebrate.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.3039699074),(114,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“I’m gonna regret it carving him up myself but someone will get him inside, probably worse…guy like him will probably get passed around like property”','Jackson\'s expression darkened. \"Yeah. Guys like Tyrone? They\'re prey inside. Especially when word gets out what he was doing to mothers.\" He glanced at his phone showing Tyrone\'s mugshot being shared across social media. \"Someone\'s gonna make him their property within a week.\"  Marcus nodded, pulling up a news article. \"Says here he\'s being held without bail. Multiple counts of assault, blackmail, distributing explicit material.\" He scrolled down. \"They\'re charging him as an adult.\"  Devon\'s phone buzzed with a message from his cop cousin. He read it, then looked up. \"He\'s in county lockup. My cousin says the other inmates already know what he did. They don\'t like guys who hurt kids.\"  The cafeteria noise swelled around them as more students watched the videos spreading online.  Linda stepped away from the window, heading toward her car. *He\'s locked up. He can\'t hurt anyone else\'s children.*','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.3049768519),(115,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*as the day goes on the principal and teachers and councillors pull us aside and get statements from all of Tyrone’s victims on behalf of the police feeling it would be easier and less stressful that way and by the time school gets out we head out and Jackson’s mom is already there no longer dressed in her skimpy red dress rather in something much more conservative*','The final bell rang at 3:15 PM. Michael walked out with Jackson, Marcus, and Devon—all of them drained from hours of giving statements to counselors and police liaisons. The parking lot was packed with parents picking up their kids.  Jackson stopped mid-step. His mother stood beside her sedan, dressed in a modest blouse and jeans instead of the tight red dress. Her hair was pulled back in a simple ponytail. She looked small, uncertain.  She raised her hand in a tentative wave when she saw Jackson.  \"Mom actually showed up,\" Jackson muttered, his voice flat.  Marcus clapped his shoulder. \"Up to you, man.\"  Jackson\'s mother took a step forward, then stopped, waiting. Her hands twisted together. *Please don\'t hate me. Please give me another chance.*  Students streamed past them, some pointing, whispering. Everyone knew now.  Jackson\'s jaw worked. He didn\'t move toward the car.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.3154513889),(116,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*as the day goes on the principal and teachers and councillors pull us aside and get statements from all of Tyrone’s victims on behalf of the police feeling it would be easier and less stressful that way and by the time school gets out we head out and Jackson’s mom is already there no longer dressed in her skimpy red dress rather in something much more conservative*','Jackson\'s mother stood beside her sedan, wearing a cream blouse and mom jeans—nothing like the tight red dress from this morning. Her hair was pulled back in a simple ponytail. No makeup. She looked older, smaller.  \"Jackson,\" she called softly. \"Can we... can we talk?\"  Jackson\'s jaw tightened. His backpack hung heavy on one shoulder. Students streamed past them, some pointing, whispering.  Marcus and Devon exchanged glances, then stepped back to give Jackson space.  Jackson\'s mother took a hesitant step forward. \"I went home. I stayed home. I threw away all those...\" Her voice cracked. \"I called a therapist. Made an appointment for tomorrow.\"  *Please say something. Please don\'t hate me forever.*  Jackson stared at her, his expression unreadable.  \"I\'m so sorry,\" she whispered. \"For everything. For making you see—\" Her hands twisted together. \"I\'m your mother. I should have protected you.\"','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.3177662037),(117,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*while Jackson’s mom talks with him I sit and wait for my own mom to pick me up*','Jackson stood frozen, staring at his mother. Several seconds passed before he spoke. \"You really stayed home?\"  \"Yes.\" She pulled out her phone, showing him location history—home address, all day. \"I didn\'t go anywhere. I swear.\"  Jackson\'s shoulders sagged slightly. \"Therapy?\"  \"Tomorrow at 2 PM. I already filled out the intake forms.\"  Marcus and Devon walked toward the bike racks, giving them privacy. Michael sat on the concrete bench near the entrance, watching the parking lot.  Linda\'s car pulled in at 3:24 PM, parking two spots away from Jackson\'s mother\'s sedan. Linda stepped out, her bandaged finger visible as she waved.  *He\'s safe now. Tyrone\'s locked up. Michael\'s safe.*  She walked toward the entrance, her eyes meeting Jackson\'s mother\'s for a brief moment. A silent understanding passed between them.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.3274305556),(118,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','*I see my mom and walk over to her*”the police ask the teachers and councillors to take our statements….guess they thought it would be easier….”','Linda turned from watching Jackson and his mother, her hazel eyes softening as Michael approached. The bandage on her finger stood out white against the steering wheel she\'d been gripping.  \"Oh honey,\" she said, her voice gentle. \"That must have been exhausting. Giving your statement, reliving everything he did to you.\" She reached out, hesitating before touching Michael\'s shoulder. *All those bruises. All those times he came home hurt.*  Her eyes scanned the parking lot—Jackson still talking with his mother, other students filtering toward cars and buses. The normalcy felt surreal after this morning\'s confrontation.  \"Are you okay?\" Linda asked. \"Do you need anything? We can stop somewhere on the way home if you want.\"  *He looks so tired. My baby went through so much.*','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.3343865741),(119,'3183071','411535','Linda (Your Mother) and Tyrone','Artmind(Spark)-iOS','“I….just wanna go home I think”*I say quietly as I roll up my sleeve revealing my bracelet of blades and take it off*”you can get rid of this if you want”*I say tired*”I…..was ready to go with Jackson if things went bad…..in the end we just leaked everything”','Linda stared at the bracelet of scalpels in Michael\'s palm, her face going pale. The thin blades caught the afternoon light—surgical steel, sharp enough to cut deep.  *He was going to use these. On Tyrone. My baby was ready to...*  She took the bracelet with trembling fingers, her bandaged hand closing around it. \"Oh Michael,\" she whispered, her voice breaking.  She looked at the school entrance where Jackson stood with his mother, then back at the blades in her hand. *So many of them were ready. If things had gone differently...*  \"Let\'s go home,\" Linda said softly. She walked to the driver\'s side, tucking the bracelet into her purse. *I\'ll get rid of it tonight. He doesn\'t need to carry that anymore.*  She started the engine, waiting for Michael to get in.  Across the parking lot, Jackson finally nodded at something his mother said. He opened the passenger door of her sedan.','正常','2026-06-04 03:53:04','2026-06-04 03:53:04',46175.3428703704);
