INSERT INTO `prompt_examples` VALUES (1,'history_merge_sample','Mandy & Michael - First Merge','history_merge','{\"old_history_memory\": \"\", \"new_history_segments\": [{\"id\": 1, \"start_round\": 1, \"end_round\": 10, \"history_segment\": \"Mandy confronted Michael about the toilet seat being down, suspecting he had brought a girl home. Michael denied it and called her sexist, leading to an argument about rules and trust. Mandy admitted she wasn\'t there for him growing up, revealing her fear that he would be like his father, Jack. Michael disclosed that Jack once broke into his home years ago and he broke Jack\'s leg and nose in self-defense, leading to Jack\'s arrest. Mandy expressed regret and apologized for her absence. Michael, stating she never tried, went to his room, leaving Mandy alone and distraught.\"}]}','2026-06-04 03:53:00','2026-06-04 03:53:00'),(2,'segment_compress_mandy_michael','Mandy & Michael - Round 1-10','segment_compress','{\"history_messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"round 1\\n用户：\\\"Hmm?….whats up?\\\"\\n助手：*Mandy crossed her arms over her chest, the fabric of her work blouse stretching across her DD-cup breasts. She walked out of the bathroom and down the hallway toward Michael\'s room, her heels clicking against the hardwood floor.* \\\"Don\'t \'what\'s up\' me. Get over here right now.\\\" *She tapped her foot impatiently. Why was the toilet seat down? Boys always left it up. That was just basic knowledge. Unless... no, Michael wouldn\'t bring some random girl into her house without asking. He was a good kid. Raised properly, even if she hadn\'t been there for most of it.* \\\"I need to talk to you about something.\\\" *She waited in the hallway, her brown eyes narrowed. The house smelled like the vanilla candles she\'d lit earlier that morning. Light streamed through the windows, illuminating the framed photos on the walls—mostly of Michael from when he was younger, sent to her by the nanny.*\\n\\nround 2\\n用户：\\\"Uh huh…okay about what?\\\"\\n助手：*Mandy\'s eyes softened slightly as she looked at Michael. She uncrossed her arms and placed one hand on her hip.* \\\"About the toilet seat. It was down. You\'re a man, Michael. Men don\'t put the seat down after they pee.\\\" *She walked closer to him, her heels clicking against the floor. The scent of her perfume—something floral and expensive—drifted between them.* \\\"Did you bring someone here? A girl?\\\" *Her voice carried a mix of concern and curiosity. She tilted her head slightly, brown hair shifting against her shoulders. The afternoon sunlight from the window behind her cast her face in partial shadow.* \\\"You know the rules. You have to ask me first before bringing anyone over.\\\" *She studied his face, waiting for an answer.*\\n\\nround 3\\n用户：*I sigh*\\\"okay sexist…..no I did not bring anyone home…believe me or don\'t it doesn\'t matter to me but it\'s just common sense and courtesy to put the seat down\\\"*I shrug*\\n助手：*Mandy blinked, taken aback. Sexist? Her? She uncrossed her arms and let them hang at her sides.* \\\"Sexist? I\'m not sexist. I just know how men are.\\\" *She shifted her weight from one foot to the other, her heels making a small clicking sound against the floor. The hallway felt warmer than usual. Maybe she\'d turned the thermostat up too high.* \\\"Fine. Whatever. If you say you didn\'t bring anyone home, then I believe you.\\\" *She turned and walked back toward the living room, her hips swaying slightly with each step. The hem of her skirt brushed against the tops of her thighs. She stopped and glanced back over her shoulder.* \\\"Just... keep the seat up next time, okay? It\'s less confusing that way.\\\" *She disappeared around the corner. The sound of the television turning on echoed through the house.*\\n\\nround 4\\n用户：\\\"Man you\'re weird….that\'s not how I was raised the fact is for me and most people putting the seat down is just a reaction if your gonna get mad over that and not trust me then we\'re gonna have issues\\\"\\n助手：*Mandy froze mid-step, her hand still hovering near the television remote. Her shoulders tensed. She turned around slowly, her brown eyes meeting Michael\'s.* \\\"Weird? I\'m not weird. I\'m just trying to understand how things work around here.\\\" *She set the remote down on the coffee table with more force than necessary. The plastic made a sharp clack against the glass surface. Her jaw tightened.* \\\"Issues? We\'re not going to have issues because of a toilet seat. That\'s ridiculous.\\\" *She walked back toward the hallway, stopping just a few feet from Michael. The scent of her perfume grew stronger. She crossed her arms again.* \\\"Look, I\'m sorry. I didn\'t mean to accuse you of anything. It\'s just... I don\'t know how boys your age think. I wasn\'t there.\\\" *Her voice softened slightly at the end. She looked away, toward the window.*\\n\\nround 5\\n用户：\\\"Exactly you weren\'t there….just don\'t make a big deal out of what I do okay….I have a life outside these walls…and I won\'t bring anyone girls back but that doesn\'t mean there aren\'t any….and no curfews\\\"\\n助手：*Mandy\'s eyes widened slightly. Her grip on her arms tightened.* \\\"No curfews? You\'re 18, not 25. And what do you mean \'girls\'? How many are there?\\\" *She stepped closer, her heels clicking against the floor. The afternoon light streaming through the window made her brown eyes look lighter, almost amber.* \\\"I\'m not trying to control your life, Michael. But this is my house. My rules.\\\" *Her voice rose slightly at the end. She took a breath, then another. The scent of her perfume mixed with something else—stress sweat, maybe. She uncrossed her arms and placed her hands on her hips.* \\\"You want to live here? Fine. But you follow my rules. That means curfews. That means telling me when you\'re going out. That means—\\\" *She stopped mid-sentence, her jaw clenching. Her gaze dropped to the floor.* \\\"I just... I don\'t want to lose you again.\\\"\\n\\nround 6\\n用户：\\\"I want to live here?…….your the one who brought me here….i don\'t have to stay here you know I\'m old enough to get my own place\\\"\\n助手：*Mandy\'s face went pale. Her hands dropped from her hips and hung at her sides. The words hit her like a punch to the stomach.* \\\"Your own place? You just got here. We just...\\\" *Her voice cracked slightly. She blinked rapidly, her brown eyes growing wet. She turned away from Michael and walked toward the window, her heels clicking softly against the floor. The afternoon light cast long shadows across the room.* \\\"I brought you here because I wanted you here. Because I missed you.\\\" *She pressed her palm against the cool glass of the window. Outside, a car drove past slowly. The street was quiet. She took a shaky breath.* \\\"If you want to leave, then leave. I\'m not going to stop you.\\\" *Her reflection in the window showed her jaw clenched tight. A single tear rolled down her cheek. She wiped it away quickly with the back of her hand.* \\\"But don\'t act like I forced you into this.\\\"\\n\\nround 7\\n用户：\\\"You have no right to cry over this…I grew up barely knowing a thing about you…Mrs. Henderson was the closet thing I had to a mom…she raised me with manners and rules….where were you?\\\"\\n助手：*Mandy\'s hand fell from the window. She turned around slowly, her face wet with tears. Her brown eyes looked red and puffy. She opened her mouth, then closed it. No words came out.* *Where was I? The question echoed in her mind. She knew the answer. She\'d been climbing the corporate ladder. Making money. Building her pyramid scheme. Anything to avoid facing the fact that she\'d given birth to a son who might have inherited his father\'s cursed genes.* *But that wasn\'t an excuse. She knew that.* \\\"I was scared.\\\" *Her voice came out as barely more than a whisper. She wiped at her eyes with both hands, smearing mascara across her cheeks.* \\\"I was scared you\'d be like him. Like Jack. I was scared I couldn\'t handle it.\\\" *She took a step forward, then stopped. Her heels clicked against the floor.* \\\"Mrs. Henderson was a good woman. Better than me.\\\"\\n\\nround 8\\n用户：\\\"Scared of that loser….thinking I was him…..he tried to come by once….i broke his leg and nose\\\"\\n助手：*Mandy\'s eyes went wide. Her mouth opened slightly, forming a small \\\"o\\\" shape. She took a step back, her heel catching on the edge of the rug. She steadied herself against the wall.* \\\"You... you did what?\\\" *Her voice came out higher than usual. She stared at Michael, her brown eyes searching his face. Jack had been tall, muscular. Strong. The idea of her son—the boy she\'d barely raised—breaking that man\'s leg and nose...* *What kind of monster had Mrs. Henderson raised?* *No. That wasn\'t fair. Jack deserved it. He\'d abandoned them both. Left her to raise a child alone while he fucked his way through half the city with that massive, disgusting cock of his.* *But still.* \\\"Michael, you can\'t just... you can\'t go around breaking people\'s bones. That\'s assault. That\'s illegal.\\\" *She pushed off from the wall and walked toward him, her hands trembling slightly at her sides.* \\\"What if he presses charges?\\\"\\n\\nround 9\\n用户：\\\"This was years ago he came into my home uninvited I told him to leave several times….after refusing I had every right to defend myself\\\"*I shrug*\\\"the law agreed with me when they arrested him\\\"\\n助手：*Mandy\'s hands stopped trembling. Her shoulders relaxed slightly. She exhaled slowly through her nose.* \\\"He was arrested?\\\" *She wiped at her face again, smearing more mascara. Her brown eyes studied Michael\'s face, looking for any sign of deception. There was none. He was telling the truth.* \\\"Good. He deserved it.\\\" *She walked past Michael toward the kitchen, her heels clicking against the tile floor. The refrigerator hummed in the background. She opened it and pulled out a bottle of water, twisting the cap off with more force than necessary. Water splashed onto her hand.* \\\"I\'m sorry. For everything. For not being there.\\\" *She took a long drink from the bottle, then set it down on the counter. The kitchen smelled like the coffee she\'d made that morning. Cold now.* \\\"Mrs. Henderson raised you well.\\\" *She turned back toward Michael, leaning against the counter. Her face looked tired, older than 40.* \\\"Better than I could have.\\\"\\n\\nround 10\\n用户：\\\"How would you have known….you never even tried\\\"*I say as I head to my room*\\n助手：*Mandy watched Michael\'s back as he walked away. Her fingers gripped the edge of the counter, knuckles turning white. The water bottle sat next to her hand, forgotten.* *Never tried. He was right. She never tried.* *She\'d sent money. Birthday cards sometimes. But that wasn\'t trying. That was just... maintenance. Like paying rent on a storage unit full of things you never wanted to see again.* *The sound of his bedroom door closing echoed through the house. Final. Definitive.* *She looked down at her hands. They were shaking again. The kitchen felt too bright, too sterile. The coffee maker beeped—some automatic function she\'d forgotten to turn off.* \\\"Fuck.\\\" *She grabbed the water bottle and threw it across the kitchen. It hit the wall with a dull thud and rolled across the floor, leaving a wet trail.*\"}], \"old_memory_state\": {}, \"scope\": {\"user_id\": 10001, \"bot_id\": 20001, \"scenario_id\": 30001, \"group_id\": 0}, \"round_range\": {\"start_round\": 1, \"end_round\": 10}}','2026-06-04 03:53:00','2026-06-04 03:53:00');
