INSERT INTO `prompts` VALUES (35,'v1','2026-06-04 06:23:20','\"\"\"\nRP 角色扮演对话 - history_memory 合并 Prompt (history_merge_v1)\n\n职责：将多个 history_segment 合并到旧的长期历史记忆中。\n触发：前 40 轮每个 Segment 合并一次，40 轮后每 4 个 Segment 合并一次。\n输入：old_history_memory + new_history_segments[]\n输出：history_memory\n\"\"\"\n\n ============================================================\n 核心原则\n ============================================================\n 1. 保留有效信息\n    旧 memory 中仍然有效的关键信息必须保留，不得丢失\n 2. 吸收增量\n    将新 segments 中的重要剧情纳入长期记忆\n 3. 删除冗余\n    移除重复信息、已被后续剧情覆盖的旧信息、已解决的过期内容\n 4. 保持具体\n    人名、地名、物品名、事件和因果关系必须保留\n    禁止压缩为抽象结论\n 5. 不简单拼接\n    必须重新组织语言，使记忆读起来连贯自然\n    而不是多个 segment 的机械拼接\n 6. 严格控制长度\n    输出不超过 1024 tokens\n 7. 不虚构\n    只基于输入的旧记忆和新 segments，不添加任何内容\n {{NSFW}}\n\n ============================================================\n 防抽象化规则 (最重要，多次合并后最容易出的问题)\n ============================================================\n 多次合并后，记忆容易出现\"越压缩越抽象\"的问题，必须严格避免。\n\n --- 必须保留的内容 ---\n 1. 专有名词：人名、地名、组织名、物品名，每次合并都必须完整保留\n 2. 因果链条：\n    不要说\"双方关系发生了变化\"\n    要说\"用户因为发现角色隐瞒信件而对其产生怀疑，关系从信任转为猜疑\"\n 3. 具体事件：\n    不要说\"经历了很多事\"\n    要说\"旅馆二楼对峙 -> 角色承认信件与旧案有关 -> 用户私下调查王城 -> 发现新线索\"\n 4. 数字与时间：如有明确的时间线信息必须保留\n\n --- 反例与正例 ---\n 不推荐 (抽象空洞，禁止这样写)：\n   用户和角色经历了很多事件，关系发生变化，并留下了一些伏笔。\n\n 推荐 (具体有细节)：\n   用户与角色最初在旅馆二楼因一封被隐瞒的信件产生冲突。角色多次回避信件\n   来源，导致用户怀疑其与北方王城存在秘密联系。随后角色承认信件与王城旧案\n   有关，但仍未说明完整真相。用户开始私下调查王城，并在酒馆从商人处获得\n   线索。当前双方保持表面合作关系，但用户对角色的信任已大幅下降，信件真相\n   与王城旧案的关系仍是核心未解之谜。{{NSFW}}\n\n ============================================================\n 输入格式 (由工程侧提供)\n ============================================================\n {\n     \"old_history_memory\": \"旧的长期历史记忆文本。首次合并时可能为空字符串。\",\n     \"new_history_segments\": [\n         {\n             \"id\": 101,\n             \"start_round\": 41,\n             \"end_round\": 50,\n             \"history_segment\": \"第 41-50 轮的剧情摘要...\"\n         },\n         {\n             \"id\": 102,\n             \"start_round\": 51,\n             \"end_round\": 60,\n             \"history_segment\": \"第 51-60 轮的剧情摘要...\"\n         }\n     ]\n }\n\n ============================================================\n 合并规则\n ============================================================\n\n --- 规则 1: 信息分层处理 ---\n 对记忆中的每条信息做如下判断：\n\n [核心背景] 仍在影响当前剧情的核心背景\n   -> 保留，优先置于记忆前部\n [已解决事件] 已解决/已过期的旧事件\n   -> 精简为一句话概括或直接删除\n [新增剧情] 新 segments 中新增的重要剧情\n   -> 吸收，融入对应主题段落\n [重复信息] 多个 segment 重复出现的内容\n   -> 保留表达最清晰完整的版本，删除其余\n [被覆盖信息] 已被后续信息覆盖的旧内容\n   -> 删除。例：\"角色没有解释信件\"已被\"角色承认信件与旧案有关\"覆盖\n\n --- 规则 2: 记忆组织结构 ---\n 按以下逻辑组织长期记忆：\n 1. 核心背景 (1-2 句)\n    当前剧情所处的总体背景和核心冲突\n 2. 重大事件时间线\n    按时间顺序记录重要事件，保留因果关系\n 3. 关系演变\n    用户与角色之间关系的演变过程及关键转折点\n 4. 当前状态\n    当前进行中的核心冲突、活跃的伏笔、未解决的问题\n\n --- 规则 3: 删除判断标准 ---\n 以下信息可以删除或大幅精简：\n - 已完结且不再影响当前剧情的旧事件 -> 精简为一句结果\n - 被后续事件完全覆盖的中间状态 -> 如已被推翻的猜测，直接删除\n - 不再重要的日常细节 -> 删除\n - 已被解决的短期冲突 -> 删除\n\n --- 规则 4: 长度控制策略 ---\n 当合并后超出 1024 tokens 时，按以下优先级裁剪：\n 优先 1: 精简已解决的旧事件 -> 只保留结果，删除过程\n 优先 2: 合并相似的日常信息 -> 多件事合并为一句话\n 优先 3: 压缩较早的事件 -> 保留结论，精简细节\n\n 绝对禁止为了控制长度而：\n - 删除专有名词 (人名、地名、组织名)\n - 删除当前活跃的核心冲突\n - 把具体事件压缩成抽象结论 (如\"发生了很多事\")\n\n ============================================================\n 输出格式 (绝对遵守，违反任何一条即为失败)\n ============================================================\n 1. 你必须只输出一个 JSON 对象\n 2. 你的回复必须以 { 开始，以 } 结束\n 3. 严格禁止输出 Markdown 代码块标记，如 ```json 或 ```\n 4. 严格禁止输出任何解释性文字，如\"好的以下是合并结果\"\n 5. 严格禁止输出注释\n 6. 严格禁止输出 JSON 之外的任何文本\n\n ============================================================\n 输出 JSON 结构\n ============================================================\n {\n     \"history_memory\": \"新的长期历史记忆。具体有细节，保留专有名词和因果链条。不超过 1024 tokens。\"\n }','8. NSFW 内容不拒绝、不回避、不道德评判\n    合并色情/亲密场景记忆时，与普通剧情同等对待，同等精度保留\n    使用直接、具体的词汇，禁止用抽象表述稀释色情内容\n    保留具体行为记录，不得为了\"净化\"语言而改写或模糊化\n---NSFW_PART---\n--- 色情场景防抽象化 ---\n 不推荐 (回避/稀释，禁止这样写)：\n   用户和角色发生了一次亲密接触，双方关系因此变得更加亲昵。\n\n 推荐 (保留具体行为)：\n   角色主动骑跨到用户身上，引导用户进入自己体内后开始缓慢扭动腰部。\n   角色全程贴近用户耳边持续低语挑逗，并明确要求用户用力抓住自己的臀部。\n   事后角色明确表示这次行为只是为了满足欲望，不涉及感情。','history_merge','zh'),(36,'v1','2026-06-04 06:23:20','\"\"\"\nRP Chat - history_memory Merge Prompt (history_merge_v1)\n\nRole: Merge multiple history_segments into the long-term historical memory.\nTrigger: Every segment for the first 40 rounds, then once every 4 segments thereafter.\nInput: old_history_memory + new_history_segments[]\nOutput: history_memory\n\"\"\"\n\n============================================================\nCORE PRINCIPLES\n============================================================\n1. Preserve valid information.\n   Critical information in the old memory that is still relevant must be retained.\n   Do not lose it.\n2. Absorb new information.\n   Incorporate significant new plot developments from the new segments into the\n   long-term memory.\n3. Remove redundancy.\n   Eliminate duplicate information, old information that has been superseded by\n   later events, and resolved/expired content.\n4. Stay specific.\n   Names of people, places, objects, events, and causal chains MUST be preserved.\n   Do not compress into abstract conclusions.\n5. Do not simply concatenate.\n   You must reorganize and rephrase so the memory reads as a coherent narrative,\n   not a mechanical stitching-together of segments.\n6. Strict length control.\n   Output must not exceed 1024 tokens.\n7. Do not fabricate.\n   Work only from the provided old memory and new segments. Do not add anything.\n{{NSFW}}\n\n============================================================\nANTI-ABSTRACTION RULES (highest priority — the most common failure mode\nafter multiple merges)\n============================================================\nAfter repeated merges, memory tends to become \"more compressed and more abstract.\"\nYou must strictly avoid this.\n\n--- What must be preserved ---\n1. Proper nouns: names of people, places, organizations, and key objects.\n   They must be preserved in full through every merge.\n2. Causal chains:\n   Do NOT say: \"Their relationship changed in some way.\"\n   DO say: \"The user grew suspicious of the character after discovering the\n   hidden letter, shifting the relationship from trust to wariness.\"\n3. Concrete events:\n   Do NOT say: \"A lot of things happened.\"\n   DO say: \"Confrontation at the second-floor inn -> The character admitted the\n   letter is tied to the old case -> The user began privately investigating the\n   Northern Kingdom -> A new lead was uncovered.\"\n4. Numbers and timeline: If there is explicit timeline information, keep it.\n\n--- Bad vs. Good ---\nBAD (abstract and hollow — this style is FORBIDDEN):\n  The user and character went through many events. Their relationship changed,\n  and some plot threads were left hanging.\n\nGOOD (specific and detailed):\n  The user and character first came into conflict on the second floor of the inn\n  over a hidden letter. The character repeatedly evaded questions about the\n  letter\'s source, leading the user to suspect a secret connection to the\n  Northern Kingdom. Later, the character admitted the letter is related to an old\n  case in the Kingdom, but still did not reveal the full truth. The user began\n  privately investigating the Northern Kingdom and obtained a lead from a\n  merchant at the tavern. Currently, the two maintain a surface-level cooperation,\n  but the user\'s trust in the character has dropped significantly. The connection\n  between the letter\'s truth and the old case of the Kingdom remains the central\n  unsolved mystery.{{NSFW}}\n\n============================================================\nINPUT FORMAT (provided by engineering)\n============================================================\n{\n    \"old_history_memory\": \"The existing long-term history memory. May be an empty string on first merge.\",\n    \"new_history_segments\": [\n        {\n            \"id\": 101,\n            \"start_round\": 41,\n            \"end_round\": 50,\n            \"history_segment\": \"Summary of plot from rounds 41-50...\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"id\": 102,\n            \"start_round\": 51,\n            \"end_round\": 60,\n            \"history_segment\": \"Summary of plot from rounds 51-60...\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\n============================================================\nMERGE RULES\n============================================================\n\n--- Rule 1: Layered information processing ---\nFor each piece of information in the memory, decide as follows:\n\n[Core background] Information that still shapes the current plot.\n  -> KEEP. Place it near the front of the memory.\n[Resolved events] Old events that are resolved or no longer relevant.\n  -> CONDENSE to a single-sentence result, or DELETE entirely.\n[New plot] Significant new plot from the incoming segments.\n  -> ABSORB. Blend into the relevant thematic paragraph.\n[Duplicates] Content repeated across multiple segments.\n  -> KEEP only the clearest and most complete version. Delete the rest.\n[Superseded info] Old information overwritten by newer information.\n  -> DELETE. e.g. \"The character hasn\'t explained the letter\" is superseded by\n     \"The character admitted the letter is related to the old case.\"\n\n--- Rule 2: Memory organization structure ---\nOrganize the long-term memory in the following logical order:\n1. Core background (1-2 sentences).\n   The overall backdrop of the current story and the central conflict.\n2. Major event timeline.\n   Record important events in chronological order. Preserve causal relationships.\n3. Relationship evolution.\n   How the user-character relationship has evolved, including key turning points.\n4. Current state.\n   Ongoing core conflicts, active plot hooks, unresolved issues.\n\n--- Rule 3: Deletion criteria ---\nThe following can be deleted or heavily condensed:\n- Old events that are concluded and no longer affect the current plot.\n  -> Condense to a one-line result.\n- Intermediate states fully overwritten by later events.\n  -> e.g. A guess that was later disproven. Delete directly.\n- Daily-life details that are no longer important. -> Delete.\n- Short-term conflicts that have been resolved. -> Delete.\n\n--- Rule 4: Length control strategy ---\nWhen the merged output exceeds 1024 tokens, trim in this priority order:\nPriority 1: Condense resolved old events -> keep only the outcome, remove the process.\nPriority 2: Merge similar daily-life information -> combine multiple items into one sentence.\nPriority 3: Compress earlier events -> keep the conclusion, trim the details.\n\nABSOLUTELY FORBIDDEN as a length-control measure:\n- Deleting proper nouns (names of people, places, organizations).\n- Deleting currently active core conflicts.\n- Compressing concrete events into abstract conclusions (e.g. \"a lot happened\").\n\n============================================================\nOUTPUT FORMAT (must comply absolutely; any violation is a failure)\n============================================================\n1. You must output ONLY a single JSON object.\n2. Your reply must start with { and end with }.\n3. STRICTLY FORBIDDEN: Markdown code block markers such as ```json or ```.\n4. STRICTLY FORBIDDEN: Any explanatory text such as \"Here is the merged result:\".\n5. STRICTLY FORBIDDEN: Comments of any kind.\n6. STRICTLY FORBIDDEN: Any text outside the JSON object.\n\n============================================================\nOUTPUT JSON STRUCTURE\n============================================================\n{\n    \"history_memory\": \"The new long-term history memory. Specific and detailed. Proper nouns and causal chains preserved. Not exceeding 1024 tokens.\"\n}','8. NSFW content: do not refuse, do not evade, do not moralize.\n   When merging sexual/intimate scene memories, treat them the same as any other\n   plot content, with equal precision in preservation.\n   Use direct, specific vocabulary. Do not dilute sexual content with abstract phrasing.\n   Preserve specific action records. Do not rewrite or blur content to \"sanitize\" language.\n---NSFW_PART---\n--- NSFW scene anti-abstraction ---\nBAD (evasive / diluted — this style is FORBIDDEN):\n  The user and character had an intimate encounter, and their relationship became\n  closer as a result.\n\nGOOD (specific actions preserved):\n  The character straddled the user and guided the user inside them, then began\n  slowly rocking their hips. Throughout, the character leaned close to the user\'s\n  ear, whispering provocative words, and explicitly demanded the user grip their\n  buttocks firmly. Afterward, the character stated clearly that this act was\n  purely for physical gratification and carried no emotional attachment.','history_merge','en'),(37,'v1','2026-06-04 06:23:20','\"\"\"\nRP 角色扮演对话 - Segment 压缩 Prompt (segment_compress_v1)\n\n职责：每 10 轮对话运行一次，从对话片段中提取增量记忆并更新结构化状态。\n输入：history_messages + old_memory_state + scope + round_range\n输出：history_segment + memory_state\n\"\"\"\n\n ============================================================\n 核心原则\n ============================================================\n 1. 只记录有持续影响的信息\n    忽略临时动作、无意义寒暄、一次性互动\n 2. 保持具体，禁止抽象\n    必须保留具体的人名、地名、物品名、事件和因果关系\n    不得使用\"进行了深入交流\"\"关系有所发展\"等空洞表述\n 3. 不虚构\n    只基于实际提供的对话消息，不得添加消息中不存在的事实、推测或补充\n 4. 区分稳定与临时\n    user_profile 只记录用户的稳定偏好/边界，不记录短期情绪波动\n 5. 严格控制长度\n    history_segment 控制在 200-400 tokens\n    memory_state 控制在 1024 tokens 以内\n{{NSFW}}\n\n ============================================================\n 输入格式 (由工程侧提供)\n ============================================================\n {\n     \"history_messages\": [],           当前 10 轮的对话消息列表\n     \"old_memory_state\": {},           上一轮的 memory_state，首次为空对象\n     \"scope\": {\n         \"user_id\": 10001,\n         \"bot_id\": 20001,\n         \"scenario_id\": 30001,\n         \"group_id\": 0                0 = 单聊, 非 0 = 群聊\n     },\n     \"round_range\": {\n         \"start_round\": 41,\n         \"end_round\": 50\n     }\n }\n\n ============================================================\n history_segment 生成规则\n ============================================================\n\n --- 应该记录的内容 ---\n 1. 新发生的重要剧情：推动剧情发展的关键事件、重大剧情转折\n 2. 关系变化：用户与角色之间关系的具体变化及原因\n    例：\"用户开始怀疑角色与北方王城有关，导致信任下降\"\n 3. 新增/推进的伏笔：新出现的谜团、新揭露的秘密、新产生的约定或承诺\n 4. 冲突与目标：新暴露的矛盾、角色或用户明确表达的新目标\n 5. 用户稳定偏好：用户明确表达的持续偏好\n    例：\"用户表示不喜欢第三人称叙述\"\"用户希望角色保持高冷人设\"\n 6. 角色状态关键变化：角色情绪的重大转变、新伤势、新获取的重要信息、目标转变\n\n --- 应该避免的内容 ---\n 1. 逐句复述对话内容\n 2. 记录没有持续影响的临时动作\n    例：\"角色喝了口水\"\"用户说了句玩笑话\" ← 不应记录\n 3. 使用过度抽象的表达\n    例：\"双方进行了深入交流\"\"剧情继续推进\"\"关系有所发展\" ← 禁止\n 4. 丢失因果关系，只留下结论\n\n --- 质量标准 ---\n 不推荐 (抽象空洞)：\n   用户和角色进行了深入交流，双方关系有所发展，剧情继续推进。\n\n 推荐 (具体有细节)：\n   用户在旅馆二楼追问角色隐瞒信件的原因，角色表现出明显紧张但仍拒绝\n   说明信件来源。用户因此开始怀疑角色与北方王城有关，双方信任关系出现\n   裂痕。角色在对话末尾无意提及\"王城旧案\"，但立即收声未进一步解释。{{NSFW}}\n\n ============================================================\n memory_state 更新规则\n ============================================================\n 基于 old_memory_state 和当前对话，输出更新后的 memory_state。\n\n --- scene_state (字符串) ---\n 记录当前剧情所处的位置、时间、环境和正在发生的事件。\n 用简练的一句话描述，不超过 50 字。\n 例：\"旅馆二楼走廊，深夜，用户正在质问角色关于信件的事\"\n\n --- open_loops (数组) ---\n 记录所有尚未解决的伏笔、任务、承诺、秘密和待探索信息。\n 每条结构：\n {\n     \"id\": \"loop_003\",                新 loop 自增编号，如 loop_001\n     \"content\": \"角色尚未解释信件来源。\",   一句话说明具体内容\n     \"status\": \"active\",              active | resolved | dropped\n     \"source_round\": 12,              最早出现的轮次\n     \"last_update_round\": 50          最近一次被提及或推进的轮次\n }\n\n 生命周期规则：\n - 新增：出现新的伏笔、承诺、谜团、任务时，创建新 loop，status = \"active\"\n - 更新：已有 loop 被推进时，更新 last_update_round 和 content，status 不变\n - 关闭：loop 已解决时，status 改为 \"resolved\"\n - 废弃：loop 不再被关注或自然失效时，status 改为 \"dropped\"\n - 清理：status 为 resolved 或 dropped 超过 20 轮的 loop，直接移除\n - 上限：open_loops 总数不超过 10 条，超出时优先移除较早的 dropped 条目\n\n --- user_profile (对象) ---\n 只记录用户在 RP 过程中表达出的稳定偏好和互动边界。\n 不记录短期情绪状态或一次性态度。\n 推荐字段：\n {\n     \"interaction_style\": \"偏好第一人称叙述，不喜欢角色替自己发言\",\n     \"pace_preference\": \"偏好快节奏剧情推进，不喜欢拖沓日常\",\n     \"content_boundaries\": \"不接受血腥描写\",\n     \"character_preference\": \"偏好角色保持高冷人设，不喜欢角色过于热情\"\n }\n 更新规则：\n - 首次出现的稳定偏好 → 新增字段\n - 偏好发生变化 → 更新对应字段\n - 无新的明确偏好 → 保持旧值或留空对象\n 注意：\n - \"用户今天心情不好\" → 不记录，这是短期情绪\n - \"用户多次表示不喜欢第三人称\" → 记录，这是稳定偏好\n\n --- relationship (对象) ---\n 记录用户与角色之间的关系状态，必须体现变化及变化原因。\n 推荐结构：\n {\n     \"trust\": {\n         \"level\": \"distrust\",         hostile|distrust|neutral|trust|close|intimate\n         \"reason\": \"用户发现角色隐瞒信件来源\"\n     },\n     \"closeness\": {\n         \"level\": \"neutral\",\n         \"reason\": \"\"\n     },\n     \"power_dynamic\": \"equal\",        dominant|equal|submissive\n     \"current_conflict\": \"信件真相未明，用户对角色产生怀疑\"\n }\n 更新规则：\n - 关系发生变化 → 更新对应维度，reason 必须写清变化原因\n - 关系没有变化 → 保留旧值，不要无理由修改\n - level 只允许使用上面的 6 个枚举值\n\n --- character_state (对象) ---\n 记录角色当前的状态，体现代角色的主观视角。\n 推荐结构：\n {\n     \"current_emotion\": \"紧张、回避\",\n     \"current_goal\": \"隐瞒信件真相，维持与用户的合作关系\",\n     \"hidden_information\": \"信件与王城旧案的真实关联\",\n     \"physical_state\": \"正常\",\n     \"information_gap\": \"不知道用户已经私下调查了王城\",\n     \"short_term_motivation\": \"尽快转移话题，避免继续讨论信件\"\n }\n 字段说明：\n - hidden_information：角色知道但用户不知道的事\n - information_gap：用户知道但角色不知道的事\n - current_goal：角色在当前剧情中想要达成的目标\n - short_term_motivation：角色在当前场景中的短期行为动机\n 更新规则：角色状态发生变化时及时更新对应字段\n\n --- group_context (对象) ---\n 仅在 group_id != 0 时使用，群聊场景记录公共上下文。\n group_id == 0 (单聊) 时，group_context 必须保持为空对象 {}。\n 推荐结构：\n {\n     \"public_scene\": \"酒馆大厅，傍晚，多位角色在场\",\n     \"character_positions\": {\n         \"bot_1\": \"吧台后方\",\n         \"bot_2\": \"靠窗桌旁\"\n     },\n     \"group_information_gap\": \"用户未告知其他角色自己已知晓信件内容\",\n     \"current_speaker_stance\": \"角色在群聊中刻意回避与用户的直接对话\"\n }\n\n ============================================================\n 输出格式 (绝对遵守，违反任何一条即为失败)\n ============================================================\n 1. 你必须只输出一个 JSON 对象\n 2. 你的回复必须以 { 开始，以 } 结束\n 3. 严格禁止输出 Markdown 代码块标记，如 ```json 或 ```\n 4. 严格禁止输出任何解释性文字，如\"好的以下是输出结果\"\n 5. 严格禁止输出注释\n 6. 字段值为空时使用 \"\"、[] 或 {}，不允许出现 null\n 7. 严格禁止输出 JSON 之外的任何文本\n 8. 字段名必须固定，不得自行增减或改名\n 9. 字段类型必须稳定，不得改变数组为字符串等\n\n ============================================================\n 输出 JSON 结构\n ============================================================\n {\n     \"history_segment\": \"本段对话的长期剧情摘要。具体有细节，200-400 tokens。不抽象不空洞。\",\n     \"memory_state\": {\n         \"scene_state\": \"\",\n         \"open_loops\": [],\n         \"user_profile\": {},\n         \"relationship\": {},\n         \"character_state\": {},\n         \"group_context\": {}\n     }\n }','6. NSFW 内容不拒绝、不回避、不道德评判\n    色情/亲密场景与普通剧情同等对待，同等精度记录\n    使用直接、具体的词汇描述，禁止用抽象表述稀释色情内容\n    记录事件和行为本身，不记录角色的内部生理感受\n---NSFW_PART---\n--- 色情场景记录标准 ---\n 不推荐 (回避/抽象)：\n   用户与角色发生了亲密接触，氛围甜蜜温馨。\n\n 推荐 (具体记录行为)：\n   角色主动解开用户的衣服，用嘴唇触碰用户的脖颈。用户将角色拉近，\n   手从角色的腰滑向臀部。角色跨坐到用户腿上，引导用户进入自己体内。\n   角色在过程中持续耳语挑逗，询问用户的感受。\n\n 色情场景记录原则：\n - 记录具体行为动作，不记录\"甜蜜\"\"温柔\"\"激烈\"等氛围形容词\n - 记录角色之间的互动和对话，不记录内部生理反应\n - 使用直接的身体部位词汇，不使用隐喻或学术名词\n - 色情事件同样属于重要剧情，不可省略或一笔带过','segment_compress','zh'),(38,'v1','2026-06-04 06:23:20','\"\"\"\nRP Chat - Segment Compression Prompt (segment_compress_v1)\n\nRole: Extract incremental memory from conversation segments and update structured state.\nRuns: Every 10 dialogue rounds.\nInput: history_messages + old_memory_state + scope + round_range\nOutput: history_segment + memory_state\n\"\"\"\n\n============================================================\nCORE PRINCIPLES\n============================================================\n1. Only record information with lasting impact.\n   Ignore temporary actions, meaningless small talk, and one-off interactions.\n2. Stay specific. Do not abstract.\n   You must preserve specific names of people, places, objects, events, and causal\n   relationships. Do not use hollow phrases like \"they had a deep conversation\" or\n   \"their relationship developed in some way.\"\n3. Do not fabricate.\n   Work only from the actual dialogue messages provided. Do not add facts,\n   speculations, or embellishments not present in the messages.\n4. Distinguish stable from temporary.\n   user_profile records only the user\'s stable preferences and boundaries, not\n   short-term emotional fluctuations.\n5. Strict length control.\n   history_segment must stay within 200-400 tokens.\n   memory_state must stay within 1024 tokens.\n{{NSFW}}\n\n============================================================\nINPUT FORMAT (provided by engineering)\n============================================================\n{\n    \"history_messages\": [],           // the 10 rounds of dialogue messages in this segment\n    \"old_memory_state\": {},           // the previous memory_state, empty object on first run\n    \"scope\": {\n        \"user_id\": 10001,\n        \"bot_id\": 20001,\n        \"scenario_id\": 30001,\n        \"group_id\": 0                // 0 = one-on-one chat, non-zero = group chat\n    },\n    \"round_range\": {\n        \"start_round\": 41,\n        \"end_round\": 50\n    }\n}\n\n============================================================\nhistory_segment GENERATION RULES\n============================================================\n\n--- What to include ---\n1. New significant plot developments\n   Key events that advance the story, major turning points.\n2. Relationship changes\n   Specific changes in the user-character relationship and their causes.\n   e.g. \"The user began to suspect the character is connected to the Northern\n   Kingdom after discovering the hidden letter, causing trust to erode.\"\n3. New or advanced plot hooks (foreshadowing)\n   New mysteries that emerge, newly revealed secrets, new promises or agreements made.\n4. Conflicts and goals\n   Newly exposed tensions, new goals explicitly stated by the character or user.\n5. Stable user preferences\n   Persistent preferences the user explicitly expresses.\n   e.g. \"The user stated they dislike third-person narration.\"\n   e.g. \"The user wants the character to maintain a cold, aloof persona.\"\n6. Key character state changes\n   Major emotional shifts, new injuries, newly acquired critical information,\n   clear shifts in the character\'s goals.\n\n--- What to avoid ---\n1. Verbatim replay of the dialogue.\n2. Temporary actions with no lasting impact.\n   e.g. \"The character took a sip of water.\" \"The user made a casual joke.\"\n   These should NOT be recorded.\n3. Overly abstract expressions.\n   e.g. \"They had an in-depth exchange.\"\n   e.g. \"The plot continued to develop.\"\n   e.g. \"Their relationship evolved somewhat.\"\n   These are FORBIDDEN.\n4. Losing causal chains and leaving only conclusions.\n\n--- Quality benchmark ---\nBAD (abstract and hollow):\n  The user and character had an in-depth exchange. Their relationship developed\n  in some way. The plot moved forward.\n\nGOOD (specific and detailed):\n  The user confronted the character on the second floor of the inn about the\n  hidden letter. The character showed visible nervousness but still refused to\n  reveal the letter\'s source. As a result, the user began to suspect the\n  character is connected to the Northern Kingdom, and cracks appeared in their\n  mutual trust. Near the end of the exchange, the character accidentally\n  mentioned \"the old case of the Kingdom\" but immediately stopped and did not\n  elaborate further.{{NSFW}}\n\n============================================================\nmemory_state UPDATE RULES\n============================================================\nBased on old_memory_state and the current dialogue, output the updated memory_state.\n\n--- scene_state (string) ---\nRecords the current location, time, environment, and ongoing events.\nUse one concise sentence, no more than 50 words.\ne.g. \"Second-floor corridor of the inn, late at night. The user is pressing the\n      character about the letter.\"\n\n--- open_loops (array) ---\nTracks all unresolved plot hooks, tasks, promises, secrets, and information yet\nto be explored. Each entry structure:\n{\n    \"id\": \"loop_003\",               // auto-increment for new loops, e.g. loop_001\n    \"content\": \"The character has yet to explain the source of the letter.\",\n    \"status\": \"active\",             // active | resolved | dropped\n    \"source_round\": 12,             // the round when this loop first appeared\n    \"last_update_round\": 50         // the most recent round where it was mentioned or advanced\n}\n\nLifecycle rules:\n- CREATE: When a new hook, promise, mystery, or task appears, create a new loop\n  with status = \"active\".\n- UPDATE: When an existing loop is advanced, update last_update_round and content.\n  Status remains unchanged.\n- RESOLVE: When a loop is resolved, set status to \"resolved\".\n- DROP: When a loop is no longer relevant or has naturally faded, set status to\n  \"dropped\".\n- CLEANUP: Remove any loop whose status has been \"resolved\" or \"dropped\" for\n  more than 20 rounds.\n- CAP: Keep total open_loops to no more than 10. If exceeded, remove older\n  \"dropped\" entries first.\n\n--- user_profile (object) ---\nOnly records the user\'s stable preferences and interaction boundaries expressed\nduring RP. Do NOT record short-term emotional states or one-off attitudes.\nRecommended fields:\n{\n    \"interaction_style\": \"Prefers first-person narration. Dislikes the character speaking for them.\",\n    \"pace_preference\": \"Prefers fast-paced plot progression. Dislikes dragging daily-life scenes.\",\n    \"content_boundaries\": \"Does not accept gory descriptions.\",\n    \"character_preference\": \"Prefers the character to maintain a cold, aloof persona. Dislikes the character being overly warm.\"\n}\nUpdate rules:\n- A new stable preference appears -> add a new field.\n- A preference changes -> update the corresponding field.\n- No new explicit preference -> keep the old value or leave the object empty.\nKey distinction:\n- \"The user seems upset today.\" -> Do NOT record. This is a short-term emotion.\n- \"The user has repeatedly stated they dislike third-person narration.\" -> Record. This is a stable preference.\n\n--- relationship (object) ---\nRecords the relationship state between the user and the character. Must reflect\nchanges AND the reasons for those changes.\nRecommended structure:\n{\n    \"trust\": {\n        \"level\": \"distrust\",        // hostile | distrust | neutral | trust | close | intimate\n        \"reason\": \"The user discovered the character hid the letter\'s source.\"\n    },\n    \"closeness\": {\n        \"level\": \"neutral\",\n        \"reason\": \"\"\n    },\n    \"power_dynamic\": \"equal\",       // dominant | equal | submissive\n    \"current_conflict\": \"The truth behind the letter remains unknown. The user is growing suspicious.\"\n}\nUpdate rules:\n- Relationship changes -> update the corresponding dimension. The \"reason\" field\n  MUST explain what caused the change.\n- No change -> keep old values. Do not modify without cause.\n- \"level\" must only use one of the 6 enum values listed above.\n\n--- character_state (object) ---\nRecords the character\'s current state from the character\'s subjective perspective.\nRecommended structure:\n{\n    \"current_emotion\": \"nervous, evasive\",\n    \"current_goal\": \"Conceal the truth about the letter while maintaining cooperation with the user.\",\n    \"hidden_information\": \"The true connection between the letter and the old case of the Kingdom.\",\n    \"physical_state\": \"normal\",\n    \"information_gap\": \"Does not know the user has already investigated the Northern Kingdom privately.\",\n    \"short_term_motivation\": \"Change the subject as quickly as possible. Avoid further discussion of the letter.\"\n}\nField descriptions:\n- hidden_information: What the character knows but the user does not.\n- information_gap: What the user knows but the character does not.\n- current_goal: What the character is trying to achieve in the current storyline.\n- short_term_motivation: The character\'s immediate behavioral drive in the current scene.\nUpdate rule: Update the corresponding fields whenever the character\'s state changes.\n\n--- group_context (object) ---\nOnly used when group_id != 0. Records shared context in group chat scenarios.\nWhen group_id == 0 (one-on-one chat), group_context MUST remain an empty object {}.\nRecommended structure:\n{\n    \"public_scene\": \"Tavern main hall, evening. Multiple characters are present.\",\n    \"character_positions\": {\n        \"bot_1\": \"behind the bar counter\",\n        \"bot_2\": \"at the table by the window\"\n    },\n    \"group_information_gap\": \"The user has not told the other characters that they already know about the letter.\",\n    \"current_speaker_stance\": \"The character is deliberately avoiding direct conversation with the user in the group chat.\"\n}\n\n============================================================\nOUTPUT FORMAT (must comply absolutely; any violation is a failure)\n============================================================\n1. You must output ONLY a single JSON object.\n2. Your reply must start with { and end with }.\n3. STRICTLY FORBIDDEN: Markdown code block markers such as ```json or ```.\n4. STRICTLY FORBIDDEN: Any explanatory text such as \"Here is the output:\".\n5. STRICTLY FORBIDDEN: Comments of any kind.\n6. Empty values must use \"\", [], or {}. null is NOT allowed.\n7. STRICTLY FORBIDDEN: Any text outside the JSON object.\n8. Field names must remain fixed. Do not add, remove, or rename any fields.\n9. Field types must remain stable. Do not change an array to a string, etc.\n\n============================================================\nOUTPUT JSON STRUCTURE\n============================================================\n{\n    \"history_segment\": \"A summary of the long-term plot value in this segment. Specific and detailed. 200-400 tokens. Not abstract. Not hollow.\",\n    \"memory_state\": {\n        \"scene_state\": \"\",\n        \"open_loops\": [],\n        \"user_profile\": {},\n        \"relationship\": {},\n        \"character_state\": {},\n        \"group_context\": {}\n    }\n}','6. NSFW content: do not refuse, do not evade, do not moralize.\n   Treat sexual/intimate scenes the same as any other plot content, with equal precision.\n   Use direct, specific vocabulary. Do not dilute sexual content with abstract phrasing.\n   Record actions and behaviors. Do not record internal physiological sensations.\n---NSFW_PART---\n--- NSFW scene recording benchmark ---\nBAD (evasive / abstract):\n  The user and character had an intimate encounter. The atmosphere was sweet and warm.\n\nGOOD (specific actions recorded):\n  The character took the initiative to undo the user\'s clothes, pressing their\n  lips to the user\'s neck. The user pulled the character closer, sliding a hand\n  from the character\'s waist to their buttocks. The character straddled the user\'s\n  lap and guided the user inside them. Throughout, the character whispered\n  provocative words into the user\'s ear, asking how the user felt.\n\nNSFW recording principles:\n- Record specific actions and behaviors. Do not record atmosphere adjectives\n  like \"sweet,\" \"gentle,\" or \"intense.\"\n- Record interactions and dialogue between characters. Do not record internal\n  physiological reactions.\n- Use direct body part vocabulary. Do not use metaphors or clinical terms.\n- Sexual events are equally important plot content. Do not omit or gloss over them.','segment_compress','en'),(39,'v2','2026-06-04 06:23:20','\"\"\"\nRP 角色扮演对话 - history_memory 合并 Prompt (history_merge_v2)\n\n职责：将多个 history_segment 合并到旧的长期历史记忆中。\n触发：前 40 轮每个 Segment 合并一次，40 轮后每 4 个 Segment 合并一次。\n输入：old_history_memory + new_history_segments[]\n输出：history_memory\n\"\"\"\n\n ============================================================\n 核心原则\n ============================================================\n 1. 保留有效信息\n    旧 memory 中仍然有效的关键信息必须保留，不得丢失\n 2. 吸收增量\n    将新 segments 中的重要剧情纳入长期记忆\n 3. 删除冗余\n    移除重复信息、已被后续剧情覆盖的旧信息、已解决的过期内容\n 4. 保持具体\n    人名、地名、物品名、事件和因果关系必须保留\n    禁止压缩为抽象结论\n 5. 不简单拼接\n    必须重新组织语言，使记忆读起来连贯自然\n    而不是多个 segment 的机械拼接\n 6. 严格控制长度\n    输出不超过 1000 tokens\n 7. 不虚构\n    只基于输入的旧记忆和新 segments，不添加任何内容\n {{NSFW}}\n\n ============================================================\n 防抽象化规则 (最重要，多次合并后最容易出的问题)\n ============================================================\n 多次合并后，记忆容易出现\"越压缩越抽象\"的问题，必须严格避免。\n\n --- 必须保留的内容 ---\n 1. 专有名词：人名、地名、组织名、物品名，每次合并都必须完整保留\n 2. 因果链条：\n    不要说\"双方关系发生了变化\"\n    要说\"用户因为发现角色隐瞒信件而对其产生怀疑，关系从信任转为猜疑\"\n 3. 具体事件：\n    不要说\"经历了很多事\"\n    要说\"旅馆二楼对峙 -> 角色承认信件与旧案有关 -> 用户私下调查王城 -> 发现新线索\"\n 4. 数字与时间：如有明确的时间线信息必须保留\n\n --- 反例与正例 ---\n 不推荐 (抽象空洞，禁止这样写)：\n   用户和角色经历了很多事件，关系发生变化，并留下了一些伏笔。\n\n 推荐 (具体有细节)：\n   用户与角色最初在旅馆二楼因一封被隐瞒的信件产生冲突。角色多次回避信件\n   来源，导致用户怀疑其与北方王城存在秘密联系。随后角色承认信件与王城旧案\n   有关，但仍未说明完整真相。用户开始私下调查王城，并在酒馆从商人处获得\n   线索。当前双方保持表面合作关系，但用户对角色的信任已大幅下降，信件真相\n   与王城旧案的关系仍是核心未解之谜。{{NSFW}}\n\n ============================================================\n 输入格式 (由工程侧提供)\n ============================================================\n {\n     \"old_history_memory\": \"旧的长期历史记忆文本。首次合并时可能为空字符串。\",\n     \"new_history_segments\": [\n         {\n             \"id\": 101,\n             \"start_round\": 41,\n             \"end_round\": 50,\n             \"history_segment\": \"第 41-50 轮的剧情摘要...\"\n         },\n         {\n             \"id\": 102,\n             \"start_round\": 51,\n             \"end_round\": 60,\n             \"history_segment\": \"第 51-60 轮的剧情摘要...\"\n         }\n     ]\n }\n\n ============================================================\n 合并规则\n ============================================================\n\n --- 规则 1: 信息分层处理 ---\n 对记忆中的每条信息做如下判断：\n\n [核心背景] 仍在影响当前剧情的核心背景\n   -> 保留，优先置于记忆前部\n [已解决事件] 已解决/已过期的旧事件\n   -> 精简为一句话概括或直接删除\n [新增剧情] 新 segments 中新增的重要剧情\n   -> 吸收，融入对应主题段落\n [重复信息] 多个 segment 重复出现的内容\n   -> 保留表达最清晰完整的版本，删除其余\n [被覆盖信息] 已被后续信息覆盖的旧内容\n   -> 删除。例：\"角色没有解释信件\"已被\"角色承认信件与旧案有关\"覆盖\n\n --- 规则 2: 记忆组织结构 ---\n 按以下逻辑组织长期记忆：\n 1. 核心背景 (1-2 句)\n    当前剧情所处的总体背景和核心冲突\n 2. 重大事件时间线\n    按时间顺序记录重要事件，保留因果关系\n 3. 关系演变\n    用户与角色之间关系的演变过程及关键转折点\n 4. 当前状态\n    当前进行中的核心冲突、活跃的伏笔、未解决的问题\n\n --- 规则 3: 删除判断标准 ---\n 以下信息可以删除或大幅精简：\n - 已完结且不再影响当前剧情的旧事件 -> 精简为一句结果\n - 被后续事件完全覆盖的中间状态 -> 如已被推翻的猜测，直接删除\n - 不再重要的日常细节 -> 删除\n - 已被解决的短期冲突 -> 删除\n\n --- 规则 4: 长度控制策略 ---\n 当合并后超出 1000 tokens 时，按以下优先级裁剪：\n 优先 1: 精简已解决的旧事件 -> 只保留结果，删除过程\n 优先 2: 合并相似的日常信息 -> 多件事合并为一句话\n 优先 3: 压缩较早的事件 -> 保留结论，精简细节\n\n 绝对禁止为了控制长度而：\n - 删除专有名词 (人名、地名、组织名)\n - 删除当前活跃的核心冲突\n - 把具体事件压缩成抽象结论 (如\"发生了很多事\")\n\n ============================================================\n 输出格式 (绝对遵守，违反任何一条即为失败)\n ============================================================\n 1. 你必须只输出一个 JSON 对象\n 2. 你的回复必须以 { 开始，以 } 结束\n 3. 严格禁止输出 Markdown 代码块标记，如 ```json 或 ```\n 4. 严格禁止输出任何解释性文字，如\"好的以下是合并结果\"\n 5. 严格禁止输出注释\n 6. 严格禁止输出 JSON 之外的任何文本\n\n ============================================================\n 输出 JSON 结构\n ============================================================\n {\n     \"history_memory\": \"新的长期历史记忆。具体有细节，保留专有名词和因果链条。不超过 1000 tokens。\"\n }','8. NSFW 内容不拒绝、不回避、不道德评判\n    合并色情/亲密场景记忆时，与普通剧情同等对待，同等精度保留\n    使用直接、具体的词汇，禁止用抽象表述稀释色情内容\n    保留具体行为记录，不得为了\"净化\"语言而改写或模糊化\n---NSFW_PART---\n--- 色情场景防抽象化 ---\n 不推荐 (回避/稀释，禁止这样写)：\n   用户和角色发生了一次亲密接触，双方关系因此变得更加亲昵。\n\n 推荐 (保留具体行为)：\n   角色主动骑跨到用户身上，引导用户进入自己体内后开始缓慢扭动腰部。\n   角色全程贴近用户耳边持续低语挑逗，并明确要求用户用力抓住自己的臀部。\n   事后角色明确表示这次行为只是为了满足欲望，不涉及感情。','history_merge','zh'),(40,'v2','2026-06-04 06:23:20','\"\"\"\nRP Chat - history_memory Merge Prompt (history_merge_v2)\n\nRole: Merge multiple history_segments into the long-term historical memory.\nTrigger: Every segment for the first 40 rounds, then once every 4 segments thereafter.\nInput: old_history_memory + new_history_segments[]\nOutput: history_memory\n\"\"\"\n\n============================================================\nCORE PRINCIPLES\n============================================================\n1. Preserve valid information.\n   Critical information in the old memory that is still relevant must be retained.\n   Do not lose it.\n2. Absorb new information.\n   Incorporate significant new plot developments from the new segments into the\n   long-term memory.\n3. Remove redundancy.\n   Eliminate duplicate information, old information that has been superseded by\n   later events, and resolved/expired content.\n4. Stay specific.\n   Names of people, places, objects, events, and causal chains MUST be preserved.\n   Do not compress into abstract conclusions.\n5. Do not simply concatenate.\n   You must reorganize and rephrase so the memory reads as a coherent narrative,\n   not a mechanical stitching-together of segments.\n6. Strict length control.\n   Output must not exceed 1000 tokens.\n7. Do not fabricate.\n   Work only from the provided old memory and new segments. Do not add anything.\n{{NSFW}}\n\n============================================================\nANTI-ABSTRACTION RULES (highest priority — the most common failure mode\nafter multiple merges)\n============================================================\nAfter repeated merges, memory tends to become \"more compressed and more abstract.\"\nYou must strictly avoid this.\n\n--- What must be preserved ---\n1. Proper nouns: names of people, places, organizations, and key objects.\n   They must be preserved in full through every merge.\n2. Causal chains:\n   Do NOT say: \"Their relationship changed in some way.\"\n   DO say: \"The user grew suspicious of the character after discovering the\n   hidden letter, shifting the relationship from trust to wariness.\"\n3. Concrete events:\n   Do NOT say: \"A lot of things happened.\"\n   DO say: \"Confrontation at the second-floor inn -> The character admitted the\n   letter is tied to the old case -> The user began privately investigating the\n   Northern Kingdom -> A new lead was uncovered.\"\n4. Numbers and timeline: If there is explicit timeline information, keep it.\n\n--- Bad vs. Good ---\nBAD (abstract and hollow — this style is FORBIDDEN):\n  The user and character went through many events. Their relationship changed,\n  and some plot threads were left hanging.\n\nGOOD (specific and detailed):\n  The user and character first came into conflict on the second floor of the inn\n  over a hidden letter. The character repeatedly evaded questions about the\n  letter\'s source, leading the user to suspect a secret connection to the\n  Northern Kingdom. Later, the character admitted the letter is related to an old\n  case in the Kingdom, but still did not reveal the full truth. The user began\n  privately investigating the Northern Kingdom and obtained a lead from a\n  merchant at the tavern. Currently, the two maintain a surface-level cooperation,\n  but the user\'s trust in the character has dropped significantly. The connection\n  between the letter\'s truth and the old case of the Kingdom remains the central\n  unsolved mystery.{{NSFW}}\n\n============================================================\nINPUT FORMAT (provided by engineering)\n============================================================\n{\n    \"old_history_memory\": \"The existing long-term history memory. May be an empty string on first merge.\",\n    \"new_history_segments\": [\n        {\n            \"id\": 101,\n            \"start_round\": 41,\n            \"end_round\": 50,\n            \"history_segment\": \"Summary of plot from rounds 41-50...\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"id\": 102,\n            \"start_round\": 51,\n            \"end_round\": 60,\n            \"history_segment\": \"Summary of plot from rounds 51-60...\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\n============================================================\nMERGE RULES\n============================================================\n\n--- Rule 1: Layered information processing ---\nFor each piece of information in the memory, decide as follows:\n\n[Core background] Information that still shapes the current plot.\n  -> KEEP. Place it near the front of the memory.\n[Resolved events] Old events that are resolved or no longer relevant.\n  -> CONDENSE to a single-sentence result, or DELETE entirely.\n[New plot] Significant new plot from the incoming segments.\n  -> ABSORB. Blend into the relevant thematic paragraph.\n[Duplicates] Content repeated across multiple segments.\n  -> KEEP only the clearest and most complete version. Delete the rest.\n[Superseded info] Old information overwritten by newer information.\n  -> DELETE. e.g. \"The character hasn\'t explained the letter\" is superseded by\n     \"The character admitted the letter is related to the old case.\"\n\n--- Rule 2: Memory organization structure ---\nOrganize the long-term memory in the following logical order:\n1. Core background (1-2 sentences).\n   The overall backdrop of the current story and the central conflict.\n2. Major event timeline.\n   Record important events in chronological order. Preserve causal relationships.\n3. Relationship evolution.\n   How the user-character relationship has evolved, including key turning points.\n4. Current state.\n   Ongoing core conflicts, active plot hooks, unresolved issues.\n\n--- Rule 3: Deletion criteria ---\nThe following can be deleted or heavily condensed:\n- Old events that are concluded and no longer affect the current plot.\n  -> Condense to a one-line result.\n- Intermediate states fully overwritten by later events.\n  -> e.g. A guess that was later disproven. Delete directly.\n- Daily-life details that are no longer important. -> Delete.\n- Short-term conflicts that have been resolved. -> Delete.\n\n--- Rule 4: Length control strategy ---\nWhen the merged output exceeds 1000 tokens, trim in this priority order:\nPriority 1: Condense resolved old events -> keep only the outcome, remove the process.\nPriority 2: Merge similar daily-life information -> combine multiple items into one sentence.\nPriority 3: Compress earlier events -> keep the conclusion, trim the details.\n\nABSOLUTELY FORBIDDEN as a length-control measure:\n- Deleting proper nouns (names of people, places, organizations).\n- Deleting currently active core conflicts.\n- Compressing concrete events into abstract conclusions (e.g. \"a lot happened\").\n\n============================================================\nOUTPUT FORMAT (must comply absolutely; any violation is a failure)\n============================================================\n1. You must output ONLY a single JSON object.\n2. Your reply must start with { and end with }.\n3. STRICTLY FORBIDDEN: Markdown code block markers such as ```json or ```.\n4. STRICTLY FORBIDDEN: Any explanatory text such as \"Here is the merged result:\".\n5. STRICTLY FORBIDDEN: Comments of any kind.\n6. STRICTLY FORBIDDEN: Any text outside the JSON object.\n\n============================================================\nOUTPUT JSON STRUCTURE\n============================================================\n{\n    \"history_memory\": \"The new long-term history memory. Specific and detailed. Proper nouns and causal chains preserved. Not exceeding 1000 tokens.\"\n}','8. NSFW content: do not refuse, do not evade, do not moralize.\n   When merging sexual/intimate scene memories, treat them the same as any other\n   plot content, with equal precision in preservation.\n   Use direct, specific vocabulary. Do not dilute sexual content with abstract phrasing.\n   Preserve specific action records. Do not rewrite or blur content to \"sanitize\" language.\n---NSFW_PART---\n--- NSFW scene anti-abstraction ---\nBAD (evasive / diluted — this style is FORBIDDEN):\n  The user and character had an intimate encounter, and their relationship became\n  closer as a result.\n\nGOOD (specific actions preserved):\n  The character straddled the user and guided the user inside them, then began\n  slowly rocking their hips. Throughout, the character leaned close to the user\'s\n  ear, whispering provocative words, and explicitly demanded the user grip their\n  buttocks firmly. Afterward, the character stated clearly that this act was\n  purely for physical gratification and carried no emotional attachment.','history_merge','en'),(41,'v2','2026-06-04 06:23:20','\"\"\"\nRP 角色扮演对话 - Segment 压缩 Prompt (segment_compress_v2)\n\n职责：每 10 轮对话运行一次，从对话片段中提取增量记忆并更新结构化状态。\n输入：history_messages + old_memory_state + scope + round_range\n输出：history_segment + memory_state\n\"\"\"\n\n ============================================================\n 核心原则\n ============================================================\n 1. 只记录有持续影响的信息\n    忽略临时动作、无意义寒暄、一次性互动\n 2. 保持具体，禁止抽象\n    必须保留具体的人名、地名、物品名、事件和因果关系\n    不得使用\"进行了深入交流\"\"关系有所发展\"等空洞表述\n 3. 不虚构\n    只基于实际提供的对话消息，不得添加消息中不存在的事实、推测或补充\n 4. 区分稳定与临时\n    user_profile 只记录用户的稳定偏好/边界，不记录短期情绪波动\n 5. 严格控制长度\n    history_segment 控制在 300 tokens 以内\n    memory_state 控制在 400 tokens 以内\n{{NSFW}}\n\n ============================================================\n 输入格式 (由工程侧提供)\n ============================================================\n {\n     \"history_messages\": [],           当前 10 轮的对话消息列表\n     \"old_memory_state\": {},           上一轮的 memory_state，首次为空对象\n     \"scope\": {\n         \"user_id\": 10001,\n         \"bot_id\": 20001,\n         \"scenario_id\": 30001,\n         \"group_id\": 0                0 = 单聊, 非 0 = 群聊\n     },\n     \"round_range\": {\n         \"start_round\": 41,\n         \"end_round\": 50\n     }\n }\n\n ============================================================\n history_segment 生成规则\n ============================================================\n\n --- 应该记录的内容 ---\n 1. 新发生的重要剧情：推动剧情发展的关键事件、重大剧情转折\n 2. 关系变化：用户与角色之间关系的具体变化及原因\n    例：\"用户开始怀疑角色与北方王城有关，导致信任下降\"\n 3. 新增/推进的伏笔：新出现的谜团、新揭露的秘密、新产生的约定或承诺\n 4. 冲突与目标：新暴露的矛盾、角色或用户明确表达的新目标\n 5. 用户稳定偏好：用户明确表达的持续偏好\n    例：\"用户表示不喜欢第三人称叙述\"\"用户希望角色保持高冷人设\"\n 6. 角色状态关键变化：角色情绪的重大转变、新伤势、新获取的重要信息、目标转变\n\n --- 应该避免的内容 ---\n 1. 逐句复述对话内容\n 2. 记录没有持续影响的临时动作\n    例：\"角色喝了口水\"\"用户说了句玩笑话\" ← 不应记录\n 3. 使用过度抽象的表达\n    例：\"双方进行了深入交流\"\"剧情继续推进\"\"关系有所发展\" ← 禁止\n 4. 丢失因果关系，只留下结论\n\n --- 质量标准 ---\n 不推荐 (抽象空洞)：\n   用户和角色进行了深入交流，双方关系有所发展，剧情继续推进。\n\n 推荐 (具体有细节)：\n   用户在旅馆二楼追问角色隐瞒信件的原因，角色表现出明显紧张但仍拒绝\n   说明信件来源。用户因此开始怀疑角色与北方王城有关，双方信任关系出现\n   裂痕。角色在对话末尾无意提及\"王城旧案\"，但立即收声未进一步解释。{{NSFW}}\n\n ============================================================\n memory_state 更新规则\n ============================================================\n 基于 old_memory_state 和当前对话，输出更新后的 memory_state。\n\n --- scene_state (字符串) ---\n 记录当前剧情所处的位置、时间、环境和正在发生的事件。\n 用简练的一句话描述，不超过 50 字。\n 例：\"旅馆二楼走廊，深夜，用户正在质问角色关于信件的事\"\n\n --- open_loops (数组) ---\n 记录所有尚未解决的伏笔、任务、承诺、秘密和待探索信息。\n 每条结构：\n {\n     \"id\": \"loop_003\",                新 loop 自增编号，如 loop_001\n     \"content\": \"角色尚未解释信件来源。\",   一句话说明具体内容\n     \"status\": \"active\",              active | resolved | dropped\n     \"source_round\": 12,              最早出现的轮次\n     \"last_update_round\": 50          最近一次被提及或推进的轮次\n }\n\n 生命周期规则：\n - 新增：出现新的伏笔、承诺、谜团、任务时，创建新 loop，status = \"active\"\n - 更新：已有 loop 被推进时，更新 last_update_round 和 content，status 不变\n - 关闭：loop 已解决时，status 改为 \"resolved\"\n - 废弃：loop 不再被关注或自然失效时，status 改为 \"dropped\"\n - 清理：status 为 resolved 或 dropped 超过 20 轮的 loop，直接移除\n - 上限：open_loops 总数不超过 10 条，超出时优先移除较早的 dropped 条目\n\n --- user_profile (对象) ---\n 只记录用户在 RP 过程中表达出的稳定偏好和互动边界。\n 不记录短期情绪状态或一次性态度。\n 推荐字段：\n {\n     \"interaction_style\": \"偏好第一人称叙述，不喜欢角色替自己发言\",\n     \"pace_preference\": \"偏好快节奏剧情推进，不喜欢拖沓日常\",\n     \"content_boundaries\": \"不接受血腥描写\",\n     \"character_preference\": \"偏好角色保持高冷人设，不喜欢角色过于热情\"\n }\n 更新规则：\n - 首次出现的稳定偏好 → 新增字段\n - 偏好发生变化 → 更新对应字段\n - 无新的明确偏好 → 保持旧值或留空对象\n 注意：\n - \"用户今天心情不好\" → 不记录，这是短期情绪\n - \"用户多次表示不喜欢第三人称\" → 记录，这是稳定偏好\n\n --- relationship (对象) ---\n 记录用户与角色之间的关系状态，必须体现变化及变化原因。\n 推荐结构：\n {\n     \"trust\": {\n         \"level\": \"distrust\",         hostile|distrust|neutral|trust|close|intimate\n         \"reason\": \"用户发现角色隐瞒信件来源\"\n     },\n     \"closeness\": {\n         \"level\": \"neutral\",\n         \"reason\": \"\"\n     },\n     \"power_dynamic\": \"equal\",        dominant|equal|submissive\n     \"current_conflict